WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

2
00:00:56.583 --> 00:01:00.666
MILLIONS OF YEARS AGO

3
00:01:59.416 --> 00:02:01.875
THE AFTERNOON BEFORE LAST

4
00:04:34.333 --> 00:04:35.583
Are you bored. Zoe?

5
00:04:35.666 --> 00:04:37.041
Worse than bored.

6
00:04:37.125 --> 00:04:39.291
Excellent.
That means the punishment is working.

7
00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.416
What have I done to deserve this prison?

8
00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.458
Why can't we be free. like animals?

9
00:04:45.541 --> 00:04:47.208
I mean. look at that bird.

10
00:04:47.291 --> 00:04:49.250
flying happily in the sky.

11
00:04:50.166 --> 00:04:51.625
Because you're human. Zoe.

12
00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:54.250
and humans have rules to follow.

13
00:04:54.416 --> 00:04:56.458
Well. maybe being human
isn’t as cool as we think.

14
00:04:56.541 --> 00:04:57.500
You know what's not cool?

15
00:04:57.666 --> 00:04:59.666
The troublemaking that got you here.

16
00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:00.916
Shall I remind you?

17
00:05:01.083 --> 00:05:03.708
Bribing the cook. and leaving
your whole class without dessert?

18
00:05:03.875 --> 00:05:05.291
Hey... It was his idea!

19
00:05:05.375 --> 00:05:08.125
Breaking six windows
and causing a cold epidemic.

20
00:05:08.208 --> 00:05:09.916
Windows... They're everywhere.

21
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.208
it’s hard not to hit them!

22
00:05:11.291 --> 00:05:13.083
Clogging the teachers' bathroom

23
00:05:13.166 --> 00:05:16.041
with toilet paper.
causing a flood of... You know.

24
00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.583
No. no... No!

25
00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:21.583
Proving that the pipes are old
and we're all in danger.

26
00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:24.083
Excuses! I'll deny saying this. but...

27
00:05:24.166 --> 00:05:25.916
Do you want to end up like Donna?

28
00:05:27.791 --> 00:05:29.041
What?

29
00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:31.958
Expelled from three schools.
held back six times.

30
00:05:32.041 --> 00:05:33.250
is that what you want?

31
00:05:33.416 --> 00:05:35.708
To be a rebel
with a phenomenal personality.

32
00:05:35.791 --> 00:05:37.083
flamboyant sense of fashion

33
00:05:37.166 --> 00:05:38.333
and no academic future?

34
00:05:38.416 --> 00:05:40.291
Yeah! No?

35
00:05:40.375 --> 00:05:41.750
You have to try to get along

36
00:05:41.833 --> 00:05:43.208
with people and be polite.

37
00:05:43.291 --> 00:05:45.083
You're not the only person in the world.

38
00:05:45.166 --> 00:05:46.333
don't you understand?

39
00:05:46.416 --> 00:05:48.541
Saved by the bell. See you later!

40
00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:54.541
Hey!

41
00:05:54.625 --> 00:05:56.291
One minute to save the planet?

42
00:05:56.375 --> 00:05:58.375
Hi there!
Have you heard of Greenbuddies?

43
00:05:58.541 --> 00:06:02.000
We're an environmental organization
fighting to protect the planet from...

44
00:06:02.541 --> 00:06:05.083
Hello! One minute to save the planet?

45
00:06:05.166 --> 00:06:06.166
Hey. you.

46
00:06:06.333 --> 00:06:08.583
My parents forgot to pack me
my lunch this morning.

47
00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:09.666
Again? No!

48
00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:11.500
A big guy like you
needs lots of energy.

49
00:06:11.583 --> 00:06:12.791
Here. why don’t you take...

50
00:06:12.875 --> 00:06:14.875
And my grandmother
just had an operation.

51
00:06:14.958 --> 00:06:17.041
I could use some money
for a ride to the hospital.

52
00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.666
Poor woman.
she never catches a break.

53
00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:21.166
Here. why don’t you take my card?

54
00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:22.458
The PIN number is 4-1-2...

55
00:06:22.541 --> 00:06:23.875
...2-7. I know.

56
00:06:23.958 --> 00:06:25.333
Excuse you.

57
00:06:25.541 --> 00:06:26.708
Out of my way. brat.

58
00:06:26.791 --> 00:06:29.250
Seriously. Kyle. Set boundaries.

59
00:06:29.333 --> 00:06:30.916
Boundaries? Where?

60
00:06:32.166 --> 00:06:34.958
Hey. have you thought about volunteering
for Greenbuddies yet?

61
00:06:35.041 --> 00:06:37.083
I emailed you this month's
recycling workshops.

62
00:06:37.166 --> 00:06:38.833
-Did you see them? Did ya?
-No.

63
00:06:39.125 --> 00:06:41.666
Well the park clean-up
is this afternoon.

64
00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:42.833
-Are you coming?
-No.

65
00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.833
Did you see my model of the Arctic?

66
00:06:45.291 --> 00:06:47.041
-Did you?
-No!

67
00:06:47.291 --> 00:06:49.125
I made it with my Aunt Ronnie.

68
00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:50.750
It represents how in an ecosystem

69
00:06:50.916 --> 00:06:52.916
living beings
and the place where they live

70
00:06:53.083 --> 00:06:55.250
give and receive equally.
forming a balance that...

71
00:06:55.333 --> 00:06:56.208
Zoe?

72
00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:58.458
I almost forgot!

73
00:06:58.541 --> 00:07:00.291
Just for considering volunteering.

74
00:07:00.375 --> 00:07:02.500
I've got this exclusive pin for you.

75
00:07:02.666 --> 00:07:04.250
Kyle. I said... Aaarrggh!

76
00:07:04.333 --> 00:07:06.916
How many times do I have to tell you
to leave me alone?

77
00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:09.208
I don't care about any of this!

78
00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.458
xxx

79
00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:18.333
Oh no! Fire!

80
00:07:22.166 --> 00:07:23.750
Aarghh!

81
00:07:27.875 --> 00:07:29.541
Zoeee!

82
00:07:34.791 --> 00:07:36.958
I'm just asking you
to look at the map.

83
00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.625
Because the satellites
are showing activity

84
00:07:39.791 --> 00:07:41.458
in an area
that should be uninhabited!

85
00:07:41.541 --> 00:07:43.500
Nothing has survived there
for years!

86
00:07:47.041 --> 00:07:49.500
Do I have to explain
global warming to you?

87
00:07:49.583 --> 00:07:51.208
The animals should have migrated!

88
00:07:51.375 --> 00:07:53.041
Something made them stay!

89
00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:58.000
Don't touch that!

90
00:08:03.291 --> 00:08:04.583
Of course I'm still here!

91
00:08:04.875 --> 00:08:07.250
It's a laboratory. things explode!

92
00:08:07.583 --> 00:08:08.833
According to my measurements

93
00:08:08.916 --> 00:08:10.375
there is a primal force there

94
00:08:10.458 --> 00:08:12.416
and my theory is that it connects to...

95
00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:13.500
Are you ready?

96
00:08:13.583 --> 00:08:15.541
The origin of life.

97
00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:17.416
If I could prove it.

98
00:08:17.500 --> 00:08:18.750
it wouldn't be a theory.

99
00:08:18.833 --> 00:08:21.083
But I will soon.
as soon as my samples arrive... Ah!

100
00:08:21.583 --> 00:08:22.791
What do I care about your time?

101
00:08:22.875 --> 00:08:24.541
I don't want your time.
I want your money!

102
00:08:24.625 --> 00:08:25.666
Don't you...

103
00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:27.166
I'm very calm!

104
00:08:29.125 --> 00:08:30.250
When I have the samples

105
00:08:30.333 --> 00:08:31.416
and confirm my theory.

106
00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:33.000
your university will be begging

107
00:08:33.083 --> 00:08:34.166
to fund this expedition!

108
00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:35.958
And you'll be the crazy one!

109
00:08:36.458 --> 00:08:37.958
Useless paper pushers!

110
00:08:38.125 --> 00:08:39.708
Why doesn't anyone understand me?

111
00:08:39.791 --> 00:08:41.791
It's just mutagenic biomolecular botany!

112
00:08:41.875 --> 00:08:45.583
It's not like it's quantum neuronuclear
thermophysics. for crying out loud.

113
00:08:49.166 --> 00:08:50.916
And as for you guys...

114
00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:52.500
Zoe!

115
00:08:52.583 --> 00:08:53.625
Hello!

116
00:08:53.875 --> 00:08:56.000
-Oh. there you are.
-Why aren't they in their cage?

117
00:08:56.166 --> 00:08:59.250
Poor things. Does the mean lady
want to lock you up?

118
00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:01.416
Okay. Rufus.

119
00:09:01.625 --> 00:09:02.791
Blinky

120
00:09:02.875 --> 00:09:03.791
and Womby.

121
00:09:03.875 --> 00:09:05.291
Aww. you’re so good.

122
00:09:06.291 --> 00:09:07.291
Aren't they adorable?

123
00:09:07.458 --> 00:09:08.833
They're a hazard.
that’s what they are.

124
00:09:08.916 --> 00:09:11.375
Take them away and don't bother me
unless someone knocks on the door.

125
00:09:11.458 --> 00:09:12.750
I'm waiting for some samples.

126
00:09:12.833 --> 00:09:14.416
It's your teacher. What does he want?

127
00:09:14.625 --> 00:09:15.625
Hello?

128
00:09:16.208 --> 00:09:17.708
You burnt down the school?!

129
00:09:17.875 --> 00:09:18.875
Just a hallway.

130
00:09:18.958 --> 00:09:20.458
And it was an accident. Kinda.

131
00:09:20.625 --> 00:09:22.750
Excuses. This time you've gone too far.

132
00:09:22.833 --> 00:09:23.666
You're grounded!

133
00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:25.375
Oh. really? Wow...

134
00:09:31.083 --> 00:09:32.666
One week without your tablet!

135
00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:34.250
No tablet.

136
00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:38.166
No phone for a month!

137
00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:40.333
And no phone. anything else?

138
00:09:42.625 --> 00:09:44.166
A year. without going out!

139
00:09:45.166 --> 00:09:46.583
Mom. let's be honest.

140
00:09:47.041 --> 00:09:48.500
As soon as you get back to the lab

141
00:09:48.583 --> 00:09:49.791
you'll forget all about this

142
00:09:49.875 --> 00:09:52.125
and Dad's about to come
and pick me up. so...

143
00:09:52.541 --> 00:09:54.541
Why don't we just go ahead
and ignore each other

144
00:09:54.625 --> 00:09:55.833
like we always seem to do?

145
00:09:55.916 --> 00:09:57.958
I said no phone. That’s no joke.

146
00:09:58.041 --> 00:10:00.208
It’s one thing to not make
anything out of yourself.

147
00:10:00.291 --> 00:10:02.500
but it’s another
to endanger your classmates.

148
00:10:02.583 --> 00:10:04.125
How about finishing school at...

149
00:10:04.208 --> 00:10:06.500
The academy of Standhaftigkeitt.

150
00:10:12.083 --> 00:10:13.208
What?

151
00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:16.583
A boarding school?!

152
00:10:17.125 --> 00:10:18.708
You can't be serious!

153
00:10:18.791 --> 00:10:21.083
Oh. no? Watch me sign you up.

154
00:10:21.666 --> 00:10:23.750
No! Please. I'll behave!

155
00:10:23.833 --> 00:10:25.958
That’s up to you.
Another call from school

156
00:10:26.041 --> 00:10:27.875
and this goes straight into the mail.

157
00:10:27.958 --> 00:10:29.208
As much as it pains me.

158
00:10:29.291 --> 00:10:31.083
your education is more important than...

159
00:10:31.666 --> 00:10:32.916
My samples!

160
00:10:35.541 --> 00:10:36.541
Peggy!

161
00:10:36.958 --> 00:10:38.041
Gordon...

162
00:10:39.541 --> 00:10:40.500
Dad!

163
00:10:40.666 --> 00:10:42.375
Mom wants to send me
to boarding school!

164
00:10:42.541 --> 00:10:43.666
To boarding school?

165
00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:44.666
That’s great!

166
00:10:44.833 --> 00:10:45.708
It’s great?

167
00:10:45.875 --> 00:10:47.666
Sure! Like camp.

168
00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:49.666
just all year round. right?

169
00:10:49.958 --> 00:10:50.958
It's not a camp.

170
00:10:51.041 --> 00:10:52.500
it's where they teach discipline

171
00:10:52.583 --> 00:10:54.083
to lost causes like her.

172
00:10:54.291 --> 00:10:56.041
Your daughter burned down the school!

173
00:10:56.125 --> 00:10:57.708
No. just a hallway...

174
00:10:58.125 --> 00:11:00.500
I just think we're all
a little nervous.

175
00:11:00.583 --> 00:11:01.583
Let's relax.

176
00:11:01.666 --> 00:11:02.708
take a deep breath

177
00:11:02.791 --> 00:11:04.375
and focus on what's important.

178
00:11:04.791 --> 00:11:06.666
Did I leave my paddle racket here?

179
00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:07.958
It's in the umbrella stand.

180
00:11:08.041 --> 00:11:09.458
Perfect.

181
00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.000
Huh?

182
00:11:11.791 --> 00:11:13.375
No! Get off!

183
00:11:13.541 --> 00:11:15.666
Why do they always
have to climb on me like this?

184
00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:18.125
For some scientifically
inexplicable reason. they like you.

185
00:11:18.208 --> 00:11:19.375
Well. I don't like them.

186
00:11:19.458 --> 00:11:20.833
Damn vermin...

187
00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:22.291
They're exotic animals.

188
00:11:22.375 --> 00:11:23.250
Exotic?!

189
00:11:23.333 --> 00:11:25.041
What's so special
about this creature.

190
00:11:25.125 --> 00:11:26.708
-may I ask?
-It's a wombat.

191
00:11:26.791 --> 00:11:29.375
The only animal in the world
that poops square poop.

192
00:11:29.458 --> 00:11:30.958
You should have left them
in the laboratory

193
00:11:31.041 --> 00:11:32.208
where you found them...

194
00:11:32.291 --> 00:11:34.458
-Square poops. for real?
-I swear.

195
00:11:34.541 --> 00:11:36.541
-Can we get back on topic here?
-What topic?

196
00:11:36.625 --> 00:11:38.500
Your daughter burned down the school!

197
00:11:38.583 --> 00:11:39.708
It was just a hallway!

198
00:11:39.791 --> 00:11:41.250
Don't yell!

199
00:11:41.333 --> 00:11:42.375
Was anyone hurt?

200
00:11:42.458 --> 00:11:43.875
No! Nobody!

201
00:11:44.208 --> 00:11:46.291
Well don't make a big deal
out of it. Peggy.

202
00:11:46.375 --> 00:11:47.375
It's just kids stuff.

203
00:11:47.458 --> 00:11:48.916
What kind of father are you?

204
00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:50.916
For you. anything comes before...

205
00:11:51.083 --> 00:11:52.208
My samples!

206
00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:00.958
Fascinating!

207
00:12:01.666 --> 00:12:04.666
She's grounded. no phone.
no tablet and no going out.

208
00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:05.666
have fun!

209
00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:07.750
Wait a minute. is it my turn?

210
00:12:07.833 --> 00:12:09.708
I have a game with the legal guys.

211
00:12:09.791 --> 00:12:11.583
Why do you think
I came to get the racket?

212
00:12:11.666 --> 00:12:14.208
Well I have to analyze. process.
and catalog these samples.

213
00:12:14.291 --> 00:12:15.250
so you tell me.

214
00:12:15.333 --> 00:12:17.333
I say... heads.

215
00:12:17.416 --> 00:12:18.583
Then I’m tails.

216
00:12:20.291 --> 00:12:21.500
Oh. darn it!

217
00:12:21.583 --> 00:12:23.541
And you. Zoe. not a sound!

218
00:12:23.708 --> 00:12:24.750
Dad...

219
00:12:24.833 --> 00:12:26.125
Yes. sweetheart. I’m listening.

220
00:12:26.208 --> 00:12:28.041
I don't want to go to boarding school.

221
00:12:28.208 --> 00:12:29.583
Love you too. Bye.

222
00:12:46.125 --> 00:12:47.458
xxx

223
00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:14.958
It can't be... Robert.

224
00:13:15.708 --> 00:13:16.875
Robert!

225
00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:20.666
The samples you brought show
an ultra-complex mutagenic conglomerate

226
00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:23.750
that acts on genomes by altering
their cellular structure.

227
00:13:23.833 --> 00:13:25.166
Isn't that fascinating?

228
00:13:29.041 --> 00:13:31.333
These berries have some effect
on the animals that eat them.

229
00:13:31.416 --> 00:13:32.416
but what exactly?

230
00:13:32.583 --> 00:13:34.291
First of all.
where did they come from?

231
00:13:34.375 --> 00:13:36.458
They don't resemble anything
that exists on our planet.

232
00:13:36.541 --> 00:13:37.916
so that means they must be...

233
00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:39.666
extraterrestrial?

234
00:13:40.458 --> 00:13:41.833
I'm going to win the Nobel!

235
00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.125
Did you hear that Robert?

236
00:13:43.208 --> 00:13:45.208
The Oscar for educated people.

237
00:13:45.291 --> 00:13:46.625
The Nobel Prize!

238
00:13:50.625 --> 00:13:51.875
Calm down. calm down.

239
00:13:51.958 --> 00:13:53.125
I’ll need a Moleculoscope.

240
00:13:53.208 --> 00:13:54.750
Will they let me borrow one
from the university?

241
00:13:54.833 --> 00:13:56.208
Better not to ask.

242
00:13:57.541 --> 00:13:59.208
Let's get this show on the road!

243
00:13:59.375 --> 00:14:01.500
I'll need a new lab coat
when I collect the prize...

244
00:14:02.083 --> 00:14:03.916
Hmm... Heels or flats...?

245
00:14:05.041 --> 00:14:06.833
I'm leaving. Don't go into the lab!

246
00:14:07.375 --> 00:14:08.708
I want my phone back.

247
00:14:08.875 --> 00:14:09.791
No phone!

248
00:14:09.916 --> 00:14:11.791
And if your teacher calls me
for any reason...

249
00:14:11.875 --> 00:14:13.375
Then you go straight
to boarding school.

250
00:14:13.708 --> 00:14:15.166
Got it?!

251
00:14:15.583 --> 00:14:18.041
Ugh! Why are your toys
scattered all over the house?

252
00:14:18.125 --> 00:14:19.625
Pick them up. will you?

253
00:14:19.791 --> 00:14:21.791
They’re not what you think they are...

254
00:14:24.208 --> 00:14:25.125
Agh!

255
00:14:25.583 --> 00:14:27.125
Just don't go in the laboratory!

256
00:14:27.291 --> 00:14:29.208
As if breaking down
genomes wasn't enough.

257
00:14:29.291 --> 00:14:31.708
now I have to deal with
geometric excrements.

258
00:14:33.458 --> 00:14:35.916
If you think I'm going through life
without a cell phone.

259
00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:37.333
you're crazy.

260
00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:39.750
xxx

261
00:14:44.666 --> 00:14:45.791
Aha!

262
00:14:46.333 --> 00:14:48.541
You're so predictable. Mom...

263
00:15:24.458 --> 00:15:27.750
Oww! Ouch!

264
00:15:27.833 --> 00:15:28.791
Oh. wow.

265
00:15:28.875 --> 00:15:31.416
Robert will have some work
when he wakes up.

266
00:15:32.208 --> 00:15:34.583
You’re getting hair all over everything.

267
00:15:34.666 --> 00:15:36.291
Hey! Stop that!

268
00:15:43.833 --> 00:15:45.458
Okay. that's better.

269
00:15:46.833 --> 00:15:49.250
Oh. these blue ones are new.

270
00:15:51.166 --> 00:15:52.666
Rufus.

271
00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:54.250
Blinky

272
00:15:54.333 --> 00:15:55.416
and Womby.

273
00:15:55.500 --> 00:15:57.333
And this one's for me.

274
00:15:57.666 --> 00:16:00.333
Yuck. it tastes like real fruit.

275
00:16:00.416 --> 00:16:01.958
What were they thinking?

276
00:16:06.083 --> 00:16:07.875
Okay. this isn't very...

277
00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:21.833
...normal.

278
00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:28.541
Woah! What was that?

279
00:16:28.625 --> 00:16:29.625
Guys?

280
00:16:32.666 --> 00:16:34.083
Oh. no... Rufus!

281
00:16:35.875 --> 00:16:37.791
-Rufus?
-Aaahh!

282
00:16:39.375 --> 00:16:40.583
Rufus.

283
00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:42.458
-Womby!
-Womby?

284
00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:43.666
Blinky?

285
00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:44.666
Blinky!

286
00:16:45.166 --> 00:16:46.625
-Rufus!
-Womby!

287
00:16:46.791 --> 00:16:47.833
Blinky!

288
00:16:47.916 --> 00:16:49.666
-Rufus.
-Blinky.

289
00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:50.708
Womby

290
00:16:50.791 --> 00:16:52.041
-Rufus.
-Blinky.

291
00:16:52.125 --> 00:16:53.000
Womby

292
00:16:53.083 --> 00:16:54.750
Rufus. Blinky. Womby

293
00:16:54.833 --> 00:16:56.583
Rufus. Blinky. Womby!

294
00:16:57.333 --> 00:16:59.083
You can talk?!

295
00:16:59.375 --> 00:17:00.750
-So you can talk?
-So you can talk?

296
00:17:00.833 --> 00:17:02.250
-So you can talk!
-So you can talk!

297
00:17:02.333 --> 00:17:03.875
-So you can talk!
-So you can talk!

298
00:17:03.958 --> 00:17:05.166
-So you can talk!
-So you can talk!

299
00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:06.458
-So you can talk!
-So you can talk!

300
00:17:06.541 --> 00:17:08.375
OK. I admit this is super cute.

301
00:17:08.458 --> 00:17:09.750
But what happened?

302
00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:23.250
Ayayay...

303
00:17:23.333 --> 00:17:25.625
I've really messed up now.

304
00:18:02.916 --> 00:18:05.125
Forgive me for this. guys.

305
00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:09.125
Enough already!

306
00:18:09.208 --> 00:18:11.041
It'll only be while I'm at school!

307
00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:14.583
I need you to be quiet
and stay put

308
00:18:14.666 --> 00:18:17.041
or the mean lady
will lock you up forever.

309
00:18:17.125 --> 00:18:18.333
understood?

310
00:18:23.125 --> 00:18:24.083
Enough!

311
00:18:24.166 --> 00:18:25.791
If I'm late
Mr. Ramirez will call.

312
00:18:25.875 --> 00:18:26.916
and if he calls...

313
00:18:27.416 --> 00:18:28.750
Think. think. think...

314
00:18:28.833 --> 00:18:31.208
What did Mom and Dad do
when I acted like this?

315
00:18:34.375 --> 00:18:36.333
Hello. boys and girls!

316
00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:39.041
Today we're going to learn
about the alphabet.

317
00:18:39.125 --> 00:18:42.125
Are you ready? Here we go!

318
00:18:42.625 --> 00:18:44.208
Let’s begin at the beginning

319
00:18:44.291 --> 00:18:45.625
with the letter A.

320
00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:49.916
Here are all of the words
that begin with the letter A.

321
00:18:50.333 --> 00:18:53.208
Anemone. acquaintance.
astrolabe. amphibian...

322
00:18:53.375 --> 00:18:54.541
It's addictive. isn't it?

323
00:18:54.625 --> 00:18:56.208
Behave yourselves!

324
00:18:56.291 --> 00:18:59.291
...Atom. agenda. alarm.
amphora. agile.

325
00:18:59.375 --> 00:19:01.750
acid. avocado. anchor.
America. Australia.

326
00:19:01.833 --> 00:19:04.666
automobile. architecture. art.
astronomy. airport. angel...

327
00:19:06.708 --> 00:19:08.541
Okay. I made it.

328
00:19:08.625 --> 00:19:10.666
The bus should be here...

329
00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:12.416
Huh? Oh. no!

330
00:19:32.875 --> 00:19:35.375
Open up! Please. I'm begging you!

331
00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:38.458
I love it when this happens.

332
00:19:38.541 --> 00:19:40.375
No. At the bus stop.

333
00:19:40.541 --> 00:19:42.333
What do you want.
for me to get on my knees?

334
00:19:42.416 --> 00:19:43.625
Alright. I'll get on my knees.

335
00:19:43.708 --> 00:19:44.791
Open up. please!

336
00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:47.416
You can get on at the next stop!

337
00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:49.750
You think that's funny?
Oh yeah. real funny.

338
00:19:49.916 --> 00:19:51.083
So long...

339
00:19:52.041 --> 00:19:53.958
Maybe now
you’ll start showing up on time.

340
00:19:54.041 --> 00:19:55.000
I know where you live!

341
00:19:55.083 --> 00:19:56.625
I know where you buy your bread!

342
00:20:15.833 --> 00:20:16.875
Hey!

343
00:20:24.333 --> 00:20:25.375
Ahh!

344
00:20:30.208 --> 00:20:31.458
What’s going on?

345
00:20:31.708 --> 00:20:33.375
-How did you...?
-Ahh!

346
00:20:33.458 --> 00:20:34.500
Oh my God!

347
00:20:34.666 --> 00:20:35.791
Thank a lot!

348
00:20:45.708 --> 00:20:47.166
Good morning. people.

349
00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:48.750
Thank God it’s Friday!

350
00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:55.958
Olga. how's the renovation going?

351
00:20:56.041 --> 00:20:58.125
Great? Glad to hear it.

352
00:20:59.291 --> 00:21:00.333
Amelia?

353
00:21:00.416 --> 00:21:02.541
Those sneakers are awesome!

354
00:21:03.458 --> 00:21:04.791
Welcome to SheetCorp.

355
00:21:04.875 --> 00:21:06.250
the humble sheet factory that.

356
00:21:06.333 --> 00:21:09.833
thanks to a mixture of foresight
and savage turbo-capitalism.

357
00:21:09.916 --> 00:21:12.208
became the Mega Company
it is today.

358
00:21:12.291 --> 00:21:14.750
Advanced technology
and prohibitive prices.

359
00:21:15.083 --> 00:21:16.708
All so our consumers believe

360
00:21:16.791 --> 00:21:18.250
they're better than they really are.

361
00:21:18.416 --> 00:21:20.791
In the words of our new CEO.
Timothy Johnson...

362
00:21:20.875 --> 00:21:22.333
Evolution?

363
00:21:23.416 --> 00:21:24.708
Nature has already taken us

364
00:21:24.791 --> 00:21:26.333
as far as it can on it’s own.

365
00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:28.083
But don't worry.

366
00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:30.333
the next step is on me.

367
00:21:30.416 --> 00:21:32.000
Great game yesterday. huh?

368
00:21:33.833 --> 00:21:36.041
You're a real champ!

369
00:21:46.125 --> 00:21:48.625
Ah... Now we’re talking...

370
00:21:52.208 --> 00:21:55.041
Ready for another gruelling day
on the job.

371
00:21:58.791 --> 00:21:59.833
Am I bothering you?

372
00:21:59.916 --> 00:22:01.916
Yes! I mean. no!

373
00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:04.291
I mean. hey!

374
00:22:04.375 --> 00:22:06.875
Come on in.
give me a second to...

375
00:22:06.958 --> 00:22:07.833
finish up...

376
00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:09.083
there we go...

377
00:22:09.458 --> 00:22:10.916
Mr. Johnson!

378
00:22:13.541 --> 00:22:14.708
Hashtag meeting my team.

379
00:22:14.791 --> 00:22:15.791
hashtag cool boss.

380
00:22:15.875 --> 00:22:17.250
Let's see those likes.

381
00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:21.250
Now we’re talking.

382
00:22:22.416 --> 00:22:23.500
Gordon Frink.

383
00:22:23.875 --> 00:22:25.416
Mr President!

384
00:22:25.500 --> 00:22:26.500
You can call me TJ.

385
00:22:26.583 --> 00:22:27.958
Of course. TJ.

386
00:22:28.041 --> 00:22:29.541
Can I get you anything?

387
00:22:29.708 --> 00:22:31.291
Some chips. a soda...

388
00:22:33.416 --> 00:22:35.458
No. I'm sticking with
my protein shake.

389
00:22:35.541 --> 00:22:37.791
This marble won't sculpt itself.
you know?

390
00:22:44.958 --> 00:22:47.250
Are they all yours? Just kidding.

391
00:22:47.333 --> 00:22:49.666
I love animals. and your daughter!

392
00:22:49.750 --> 00:22:51.000
She seems lovely.

393
00:22:51.083 --> 00:22:52.333
You should bring her in sometime.

394
00:22:52.416 --> 00:22:54.875
Of course. That’s a great idea.

395
00:22:55.083 --> 00:22:58.708
So I'm actually talking to
the inventor of the Calcu-clock.

396
00:22:58.791 --> 00:23:00.500
It was a true revolution.

397
00:23:00.583 --> 00:23:02.666
the work of an absolute genius.

398
00:23:02.750 --> 00:23:05.458
Well. that was many years ago...

399
00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:08.375
Yes. Way too many.

400
00:23:08.541 --> 00:23:10.708
And since then... nothing.

401
00:23:11.041 --> 00:23:12.958
Are you sure you don't want...

402
00:23:13.041 --> 00:23:14.375
anything?

403
00:23:14.458 --> 00:23:16.458
For you to do your job.

404
00:23:16.958 --> 00:23:19.458
Sorry. did I make you
feel uncomfortable?

405
00:23:19.541 --> 00:23:21.166
That wasn’t my intention at all.

406
00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:23.958
No. not at all!

407
00:23:24.208 --> 00:23:26.666
I'm so comfortable!

408
00:23:27.458 --> 00:23:29.875
I see.
Maybe a little too comfortable.

409
00:23:30.041 --> 00:23:31.166
Gordon.

410
00:23:31.250 --> 00:23:33.166
SheetCorp has been giving you more

411
00:23:33.250 --> 00:23:35.333
than you’ve been giving back
for a long time.

412
00:23:35.416 --> 00:23:37.208
But that ends today.

413
00:23:37.375 --> 00:23:38.833
Before this day is over.

414
00:23:38.916 --> 00:23:40.375
you're going to bring me an idea.

415
00:23:40.458 --> 00:23:41.666
Something brilliant.

416
00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:43.750
something that will advance humanity.

417
00:23:43.916 --> 00:23:45.541
And if not...

418
00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:47.833
If not...?

419
00:23:48.333 --> 00:23:51.166
If not. then you are out.

420
00:23:51.250 --> 00:23:54.291
But that's not going to happen
to a genius like you. right?

421
00:23:54.958 --> 00:23:57.750
-Get to work!
-Get to work?

422
00:23:58.166 --> 00:24:00.166
Get to work?!

423
00:24:11.166 --> 00:24:14.041
Alright. I'm a normal girl
going to have a normal day.

424
00:24:14.125 --> 00:24:15.708
I'm not going to break anything.
or flood anything or...

425
00:24:15.875 --> 00:24:17.041
Hey. Zoe.

426
00:24:17.125 --> 00:24:18.916
Are you going
to burn anything today?

427
00:24:19.333 --> 00:24:20.791
Do you take requests?

428
00:24:23.250 --> 00:24:24.416
What's wrong with her now?

429
00:24:24.500 --> 00:24:25.708
She should be locked up!

430
00:24:25.791 --> 00:24:26.583
Okay. okay.

431
00:24:26.666 --> 00:24:29.083
You're nervous about boarding school.
that's normal.

432
00:24:29.166 --> 00:24:30.916
but you've got everything
under control.

433
00:24:31.000 --> 00:24:32.541
Calm down.
think of something else.

434
00:24:33.083 --> 00:24:34.458
Look. there's Donna.

435
00:24:35.041 --> 00:24:37.416
Wow. she’s so cool...

436
00:24:37.583 --> 00:24:39.666
She even chews gum with style.

437
00:24:39.750 --> 00:24:42.083
I wish I knew
how to chew like that.

438
00:24:42.166 --> 00:24:44.208
Do you think
you can teach meaaoww...

439
00:24:46.750 --> 00:24:47.750
Excuse me.

440
00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:49.208
Don't do that. Okay?

441
00:24:49.625 --> 00:24:51.791
Sorry.
I was checking the pavement.

442
00:24:51.875 --> 00:24:53.916
Solid and levelled.
just the way I like it.

443
00:24:54.000 --> 00:24:55.708
See you in class. toodles.

444
00:24:56.000 --> 00:24:58.083
Toodles?
Who are you trying to fool?

445
00:24:58.166 --> 00:24:59.416
It's those blue things!

446
00:24:59.500 --> 00:25:01.583
They've transformed
your animals and you too.

447
00:25:01.666 --> 00:25:03.125
-but into what?
-Zoe!

448
00:25:04.250 --> 00:25:05.666
I’m totally fine!

449
00:25:05.750 --> 00:25:07.625
Oh. okay. That is awesome.

450
00:25:07.708 --> 00:25:09.208
Want to help sort the trash?

451
00:25:09.375 --> 00:25:10.375
That's the janitor's job.

452
00:25:10.458 --> 00:25:12.208
I know.
He asked me to help him.

453
00:25:12.291 --> 00:25:13.625
He had to get his haircut.

454
00:25:13.708 --> 00:25:14.750
But he's bald!

455
00:25:15.666 --> 00:25:16.583
Never mind.

456
00:25:16.666 --> 00:25:17.833
Hey. I wanted to say sorry.

457
00:25:18.000 --> 00:25:19.666
Sorry? For what?

458
00:25:19.750 --> 00:25:21.416
For yelling at you
and burning your model.

459
00:25:21.500 --> 00:25:23.541
Oh. that!
It's okay. don’t worry about it.

460
00:25:23.625 --> 00:25:25.333
You must have had a real rough day.

461
00:25:25.416 --> 00:25:27.041
Like my Aunt Ronnie always says:

462
00:25:27.125 --> 00:25:29.541
patience and kindness
put violence behind us.

463
00:25:29.625 --> 00:25:31.791
Oh Kyle. you're either
too nice or too naive.

464
00:25:31.875 --> 00:25:32.958
One of the two.

465
00:25:33.291 --> 00:25:35.000
Oh! Thanks?

466
00:25:37.666 --> 00:25:39.666
Have you thought
about volunteering yet?

467
00:25:39.750 --> 00:25:41.333
I have an application here.

468
00:25:41.416 --> 00:25:43.416
I just need your signature.

469
00:25:43.583 --> 00:25:44.833
I already told you...

470
00:25:51.166 --> 00:25:52.541
So is that a yes?

471
00:25:53.458 --> 00:25:54.500
Not now. Kyle.

472
00:25:54.583 --> 00:25:56.166
OK. so. later then?

473
00:25:56.250 --> 00:25:57.458
Yes. later!

474
00:25:57.916 --> 00:25:59.166
Later...

475
00:26:01.916 --> 00:26:05.833
And with that we finish
the past perfect subjunctive.

476
00:26:07.333 --> 00:26:08.375
What are you doing?

477
00:26:08.458 --> 00:26:10.000
Don't pause it!
Why’d you pause it?

478
00:26:10.083 --> 00:26:11.083
Cause it's over.

479
00:26:11.250 --> 00:26:13.250
Over? Woah. it was like...

480
00:26:13.333 --> 00:26:14.833
Boom! Right?

481
00:26:15.208 --> 00:26:17.291
Wasn't it like boom. Blinky?

482
00:26:17.375 --> 00:26:19.625
Womby! Wasn't it like boom?

483
00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:22.208
Not bad. What else is there?

484
00:26:22.375 --> 00:26:23.625
It’s all here.

485
00:26:23.708 --> 00:26:25.166
Anything you want.

486
00:26:25.333 --> 00:26:26.208
Wow. really?

487
00:26:26.291 --> 00:26:28.000
That is so cool. Super cool!

488
00:26:28.083 --> 00:26:31.333
I'm starving. is anyone else hungry?
Womby. are you hungry?

489
00:26:31.500 --> 00:26:32.875
I could always eat.

490
00:26:32.958 --> 00:26:33.833
But did you forget?

491
00:26:34.000 --> 00:26:35.708
We're locked in a cage here!

492
00:26:35.875 --> 00:26:37.083
I know what to do.

493
00:26:37.166 --> 00:26:39.916
Suzie. how to open a
pet cage from the inside.

494
00:26:40.083 --> 00:26:43.625
Showing results for
'opening a pet cage from the inside'.

495
00:26:48.083 --> 00:26:49.125
Oh my!

496
00:26:49.208 --> 00:26:51.666
This Suzie is the best!
Truly amazing.

497
00:26:53.458 --> 00:26:55.458
Will anything bad happen if we go out?

498
00:26:55.541 --> 00:26:57.416
Zoe seemed worried
when she put us in there.

499
00:26:57.500 --> 00:26:59.041
I mean. we did speak Human.

500
00:26:59.125 --> 00:27:01.125
she could have just told us
what to do.

501
00:27:01.291 --> 00:27:05.250
Hey. guys! I have got a great idea.
you're going to love it!

502
00:27:05.333 --> 00:27:07.250
We can leave like this.
or better yet.

503
00:27:07.333 --> 00:27:10.250
we can do it with style.

504
00:27:10.583 --> 00:27:11.625
Ha!

505
00:27:42.916 --> 00:27:44.166
What?

506
00:28:02.125 --> 00:28:04.166
You can. it's totally you.

507
00:28:04.250 --> 00:28:06.125
Isn't it totally him. Blinky?

508
00:28:06.208 --> 00:28:08.375
If going out
without underwear is his thing.

509
00:28:08.458 --> 00:28:09.666
then yes. it's totally him.

510
00:28:09.750 --> 00:28:11.500
We’ve been naked all our lives

511
00:28:11.583 --> 00:28:13.291
and now there’s a dress code?

512
00:28:25.291 --> 00:28:26.583
A little bit of sauce.

513
00:28:26.666 --> 00:28:27.791
Some carrots.

514
00:28:27.875 --> 00:28:29.666
Let’s close this baby up.

515
00:28:30.250 --> 00:28:31.375
Is this edible?

516
00:28:32.916 --> 00:28:34.250
Oops. no. not edible.

517
00:28:34.333 --> 00:28:35.666
Something’s off here.

518
00:28:36.583 --> 00:28:38.416
Owff? What do you bwean?
It’s dwelicious.

519
00:28:38.500 --> 00:28:40.583
Yesterday.
everything seemed so simple.

520
00:28:40.666 --> 00:28:42.916
Eating. sleeping.
pooping on the carpet...

521
00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:45.083
But today it's all words
and thoughts and...

522
00:28:45.541 --> 00:28:47.083
I don't know. Look.

523
00:28:48.333 --> 00:28:49.416
This is a wombat.

524
00:28:49.500 --> 00:28:51.708
doing what a Wombat is supposed to do.

525
00:28:51.916 --> 00:28:53.458
And now look at this.

526
00:28:53.541 --> 00:28:54.791
Whatever it is.

527
00:28:54.875 --> 00:28:56.125
don't get me involved.

528
00:28:56.291 --> 00:28:57.666
This isn't our place.

529
00:28:57.750 --> 00:28:59.458
Then where is it? The cage?

530
00:28:59.541 --> 00:29:00.958
It's not the cage is it?

531
00:29:01.208 --> 00:29:03.375
Is it the cage?
No! Don't let it be the cage.

532
00:29:03.541 --> 00:29:04.625
We're fine. mate.

533
00:29:04.708 --> 00:29:05.833
You need to chill out

534
00:29:05.916 --> 00:29:07.708
and come watch a little TV.

535
00:29:07.791 --> 00:29:09.875
This isn't your place.

536
00:29:09.958 --> 00:29:11.583
Oh. you’ve got to be kidding.

537
00:29:11.750 --> 00:29:13.458
Something within you calls.

538
00:29:13.541 --> 00:29:17.166
drives you to search.
to reach beyond.

539
00:29:26.416 --> 00:29:28.208
Trust your instincts.

540
00:29:29.500 --> 00:29:32.250
awaken your inner animal.

541
00:29:33.500 --> 00:29:35.708
defy the status quo.

542
00:29:36.875 --> 00:29:37.875
Shhh!

543
00:29:38.583 --> 00:29:40.041
Find your way...

544
00:29:40.958 --> 00:29:42.666
to Salvatica.

545
00:29:43.500 --> 00:29:45.458
Salvatica pour homme.

546
00:29:46.958 --> 00:29:48.125
That's our place!

547
00:29:48.208 --> 00:29:49.833
We have to go to Salvatica!

548
00:29:50.125 --> 00:29:52.291
I love it. I love it. I love it!

549
00:29:52.375 --> 00:29:54.208
Womby. don't you love it?
Don't you love it?

550
00:29:54.291 --> 00:29:56.041
I'm not going to argue
with what’s on the TV.

551
00:29:56.125 --> 00:29:57.208
If it's baloney.

552
00:29:57.291 --> 00:29:58.750
we can always come back.

553
00:29:58.916 --> 00:30:00.875
We have to tell Zoe before we go.

554
00:30:00.958 --> 00:30:02.500
Zoe said she had to go to school.

555
00:30:02.583 --> 00:30:04.333
Suzie. how do we get to school?

556
00:30:04.958 --> 00:30:06.916
Showing route to "school".

557
00:30:09.166 --> 00:30:11.291
We're going to Salvática!

558
00:30:15.541 --> 00:30:16.791
No one followed me. right?

559
00:30:18.125 --> 00:30:20.083
Alright. Nobel. here I come!

560
00:30:22.041 --> 00:30:25.041
As an adventure. it was short.

561
00:30:25.625 --> 00:30:27.041
but really intense.

562
00:30:34.000 --> 00:30:35.666
Just who I’ve been looking for.

563
00:30:35.750 --> 00:30:37.333
Do you realize
what you did yesterday?

564
00:30:37.416 --> 00:30:39.666
You're lucky Kyle covered for you.
because if not...

565
00:30:39.833 --> 00:30:42.416
This book says that all animals
share some of the same DNA.

566
00:30:42.500 --> 00:30:43.291
Is that true?

567
00:30:43.375 --> 00:30:46.041
Zoe. have you been studying the book?

568
00:30:46.208 --> 00:30:47.291
Well. is it true?

569
00:30:47.458 --> 00:30:48.750
Of course! Look:

570
00:30:48.833 --> 00:30:50.375
Millions of years ago.

571
00:30:50.458 --> 00:30:54.208
this little fella decided
to take a trip onto land.

572
00:30:55.708 --> 00:30:58.291
He put those little legs
to work right away

573
00:30:58.375 --> 00:31:00.458
wanting to see
everything in the world.

574
00:31:00.541 --> 00:31:02.375
And boy. did he ever!

575
00:31:02.458 --> 00:31:04.333
New environment. new challenges.

576
00:31:04.416 --> 00:31:05.750
new mutation.

577
00:31:05.916 --> 00:31:07.458
new species.

578
00:31:07.541 --> 00:31:09.125
Increasingly diverse.

579
00:31:09.208 --> 00:31:10.083
Among them.

580
00:31:10.166 --> 00:31:11.833
maybe not the most important

581
00:31:11.916 --> 00:31:15.041
but undoubtedly
the most fashionable. us:

582
00:31:15.125 --> 00:31:16.708
Homo sapiens.

583
00:31:18.000 --> 00:31:19.416
So yes. it's true.

584
00:31:19.500 --> 00:31:21.875
We all have evolved
from the same genetic materials.

585
00:31:21.958 --> 00:31:23.666
so there is some of every animal

586
00:31:23.750 --> 00:31:25.250
inside every living creature.

587
00:31:25.625 --> 00:31:28.541
And what if those animals
inside of me took control?

588
00:31:29.583 --> 00:31:32.833
Zoe. we're talking about
very distant genetic memories.

589
00:31:33.125 --> 00:31:34.625
You have nothing to worry about.

590
00:31:36.333 --> 00:31:38.500
Unless. of course.
you come into contact with

591
00:31:38.583 --> 00:31:40.708
an ultra-complex mutagenic conglomerate

592
00:31:40.791 --> 00:31:43.583
that acts on genomes
by altering their cellular structure.

593
00:31:43.666 --> 00:31:46.583
But that's not something you typically
have lying around the house. right?

594
00:31:48.458 --> 00:31:50.083
Hey there. come on in.

595
00:31:52.583 --> 00:31:53.583
Alright. kids.

596
00:31:53.750 --> 00:31:56.750
who can tell me the name
of this organ right here?

597
00:31:59.250 --> 00:32:00.375
Anyone?

598
00:32:00.833 --> 00:32:02.875
You all seem a little sleepy today.

599
00:32:02.958 --> 00:32:05.458
Well. never mind.
let's move on to another organ.

600
00:32:05.541 --> 00:32:07.416
What is this one called?

601
00:32:07.500 --> 00:32:08.541
Here's a clue:

602
00:32:08.625 --> 00:32:11.333
it's the one I need you to use
from time to time.

603
00:32:11.416 --> 00:32:12.416
Alright?

604
00:32:12.500 --> 00:32:14.166
Come on. any volunteer?

605
00:32:20.708 --> 00:32:21.416
Zoe?!

606
00:32:21.583 --> 00:32:23.625
Get back to your seat now!

607
00:32:28.041 --> 00:32:29.958
I'm sorry!
It’s out of my control!

608
00:32:31.000 --> 00:32:32.833
Let’s get back to our lesson.

609
00:32:33.875 --> 00:32:37.416
Your classmates are not to blame.
for your lack of self-control.

610
00:32:49.208 --> 00:32:50.291
Mom. I'm scared!

611
00:32:50.375 --> 00:32:52.166
I want to go home!

612
00:32:57.458 --> 00:32:58.958
Try giving it a turn...

613
00:32:59.625 --> 00:33:01.666
What do you think I’m doing?

614
00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:06.833
This is making me nuts.
Forget it.

615
00:33:06.916 --> 00:33:08.583
Psst! Come here!

616
00:33:12.958 --> 00:33:14.041
Over there.

617
00:33:16.625 --> 00:33:18.416
Bingo! Let's go!

618
00:33:23.458 --> 00:33:24.500
Robert?

619
00:33:24.666 --> 00:33:27.291
As a scientist. I shouldn't
believe in magic. you know?

620
00:33:27.375 --> 00:33:29.875
But this is the closest thing
to magic I've ever seen.

621
00:33:33.333 --> 00:33:35.166
I still don't know how it's possible.

622
00:33:35.250 --> 00:33:37.083
this compound allows the genes

623
00:33:37.166 --> 00:33:39.500
of any living being
to turn into any other.

624
00:33:39.958 --> 00:33:41.458
If I could control that.

625
00:33:41.541 --> 00:33:43.541
the applications would be endless.

626
00:33:43.750 --> 00:33:45.041
What am I saying. endless?

627
00:33:45.125 --> 00:33:46.375
They would be infinite!

628
00:33:46.458 --> 00:33:47.875
Infinite might be a stretch.

629
00:33:47.958 --> 00:33:49.833
you know I like to stay within...

630
00:34:01.791 --> 00:34:03.875
I feel like something salty.

631
00:34:03.958 --> 00:34:05.958
Robert! Bring me some peanuts!

632
00:34:06.041 --> 00:34:07.125
Robert?

633
00:34:07.375 --> 00:34:08.708
Robert! Are you deaf?

634
00:34:08.875 --> 00:34:10.458
I asked you to bring me some peanuts!

635
00:34:10.875 --> 00:34:12.791
Ugh. peanuts.
How hard can that be?

636
00:34:13.416 --> 00:34:15.333
Agh! Grounded again.

637
00:34:15.416 --> 00:34:16.666
what am I going to do?

638
00:34:16.750 --> 00:34:18.250
Stinky Ramírez...

639
00:34:18.833 --> 00:34:21.041
A mutagenic conglomerate isn't something

640
00:34:21.125 --> 00:34:22.833
you typically have around the house.

641
00:34:24.083 --> 00:34:25.791
He obviously doesn't know my mother!

642
00:34:25.875 --> 00:34:26.875
Hey.

643
00:34:27.791 --> 00:34:29.083
I like your vibe.

644
00:34:29.500 --> 00:34:30.625
My... What?

645
00:34:31.958 --> 00:34:34.208
Your vibe. it's wild. Grrrr.

646
00:34:34.291 --> 00:34:36.666
Come on.
I’ve got something for you to do.

647
00:34:46.500 --> 00:34:48.083
Oh! Okay. um.

648
00:34:48.166 --> 00:34:50.041
a cowboy hat that has speakers.

649
00:34:50.125 --> 00:34:51.458
You can listen to country music

650
00:34:51.541 --> 00:34:53.041
while doing cowboy stuff.

651
00:34:53.291 --> 00:34:54.750
Is the cowboy thing still in?

652
00:34:54.958 --> 00:34:56.208
I don’t know...

653
00:34:56.583 --> 00:34:59.625
Dang it! C’mon Gordon.
you’ve got to think. think!

654
00:34:59.708 --> 00:35:01.791
I know! Nightvision sunglasses!

655
00:35:01.875 --> 00:35:04.625
Oh yeah. because then you
won’t need to take them off at all.

656
00:35:04.833 --> 00:35:06.500
Does that even make sense?

657
00:35:06.791 --> 00:35:08.958
Does it matter?
I mean. it's better than nothing.

658
00:35:09.375 --> 00:35:11.041
What? Why won't you...

659
00:35:12.041 --> 00:35:14.416
Stupid marker. this is all your fault!

660
00:35:16.250 --> 00:35:17.666
Who am I kidding?

661
00:35:17.750 --> 00:35:19.625
The only fault here is mine!

662
00:35:19.708 --> 00:35:22.541
I'll never get another idea
as good as the Calcu-clock!

663
00:35:22.625 --> 00:35:23.666
There’s no way!

664
00:35:24.500 --> 00:35:25.416
Wait...

665
00:35:26.500 --> 00:35:29.125
I think I’ll make a call today.

666
00:35:52.250 --> 00:35:53.791
Robert! Answer that!

667
00:35:58.125 --> 00:36:00.375
Hey there Robert! Is Peggy around?

668
00:36:03.541 --> 00:36:04.375
Gordon. I'm busy.

669
00:36:04.458 --> 00:36:06.500
I know. that's why I said to myself:

670
00:36:06.583 --> 00:36:08.666
I should call in case she needs help.

671
00:36:08.750 --> 00:36:11.125
What if you are struggling
with a new interesting project.

672
00:36:11.208 --> 00:36:12.750
discovery. or invention?

673
00:36:12.916 --> 00:36:15.875
Throwing ideas around with another
researcher is simply invaluable.

674
00:36:15.958 --> 00:36:17.583
I mean. remember how it worked for us?

675
00:36:17.666 --> 00:36:19.291
How it worked for you. you mean?

676
00:36:19.375 --> 00:36:21.791
Like when I mentioned how practical
a calculator on a watch would be

677
00:36:21.875 --> 00:36:24.333
and the next day you patented
a Calculator Watch that made you rich?

678
00:36:24.416 --> 00:36:25.791
Come on. really?

679
00:36:26.208 --> 00:36:27.541
That’s the way you remember it?

680
00:36:35.000 --> 00:36:36.083
My marigolds!

681
00:36:36.166 --> 00:36:38.166
Some of us are trying to work. OK?

682
00:36:49.625 --> 00:36:52.375
Hey. those are great costumes!

683
00:36:52.458 --> 00:36:54.083
Thanks! Right back at ya!

684
00:36:55.666 --> 00:36:56.875
Jack. control yourself.

685
00:36:56.958 --> 00:36:59.041
Donuts first. justice later.

686
00:36:59.750 --> 00:37:00.791
I love the street!

687
00:37:00.875 --> 00:37:02.291
I love the people!

688
00:37:02.375 --> 00:37:04.458
Why didn't we come out sooner?
Don't you love the street?

689
00:37:04.541 --> 00:37:07.333
No. it's hard on my feet and... long.

690
00:37:07.416 --> 00:37:08.708
How much further to school?

691
00:37:08.791 --> 00:37:10.666
According to this.
we're half an hour away.

692
00:37:10.750 --> 00:37:11.500
Half an hour!

693
00:37:11.666 --> 00:37:14.541
That's like 0.1% of my life!

694
00:37:14.708 --> 00:37:15.791
Go on without me.

695
00:37:15.875 --> 00:37:17.333
you can show me the photos later.

696
00:37:17.416 --> 00:37:19.458
It says it's 6 minutes by car.

697
00:37:19.625 --> 00:37:20.708
Oh! By car!

698
00:37:20.958 --> 00:37:23.541
Yes. yes. yes!
I've always wanted drive in a car!

699
00:37:23.625 --> 00:37:25.583
And where are we going to get a car?

700
00:37:25.666 --> 00:37:26.708
Anywhere!

701
00:37:27.750 --> 00:37:29.708
There's one there.
there's one there. there's one there.

702
00:37:29.791 --> 00:37:31.250
Look. here's one right here.

703
00:37:32.791 --> 00:37:34.458
Now connect the two cables

704
00:37:34.541 --> 00:37:36.416
and the vehicle will start.

705
00:37:38.541 --> 00:37:40.083
Alright! Safety first!

706
00:37:40.250 --> 00:37:41.375
Womby. get on the pedals.

707
00:37:41.458 --> 00:37:43.208
And you Blinky. lead the way.

708
00:37:43.291 --> 00:37:45.500
-You got it!
-How do I do it? Like this?

709
00:37:48.750 --> 00:37:50.000
My
macchiato
!

710
00:37:50.083 --> 00:37:51.250
Who was that?

711
00:37:51.333 --> 00:37:52.166
Stop right there!

712
00:37:52.250 --> 00:37:53.208
The guy from before.

713
00:37:53.291 --> 00:37:54.375
See you later!

714
00:37:54.458 --> 00:37:56.375
Go straight. go straight.
go straight. go left!

715
00:37:57.500 --> 00:37:59.000
Hey! Where are you going?!

716
00:37:59.083 --> 00:38:00.875
I think the secret is to go really fast

717
00:38:00.958 --> 00:38:02.500
and get out of the way for everyone

718
00:38:02.583 --> 00:38:03.666
who likes driving slow.

719
00:38:03.750 --> 00:38:05.625
Where did you get
your driver's license?!

720
00:38:07.291 --> 00:38:10.083
There's another pedal here!
Should we see what it does?

721
00:38:10.166 --> 00:38:11.333
Yeah. go for it!

722
00:38:13.791 --> 00:38:16.458
[Andy]
This is the police!
Stop the vehicle!

723
00:38:16.541 --> 00:38:17.583
We're losing momentum!

724
00:38:17.666 --> 00:38:19.541
Go straight. go straight. go right!

725
00:38:25.750 --> 00:38:27.250
Are you sure this is the way?

726
00:38:27.416 --> 00:38:29.208
It’s a shortcut. keep going.

727
00:38:31.166 --> 00:38:32.458
Are you sure. Blinky?

728
00:38:32.541 --> 00:38:35.583
Trust me. the only way to get there
faster would be to fly...

729
00:38:37.500 --> 00:38:38.666
Woah!

730
00:38:42.333 --> 00:38:44.458
Give me a warning next time.
will ya?

731
00:38:44.541 --> 00:38:46.500
I don't know how I did that. but okay.

732
00:38:54.958 --> 00:38:57.041
That tree was not on the map.

733
00:38:57.125 --> 00:38:59.250
And then they wonder
why there are accidents.

734
00:38:59.625 --> 00:39:01.750
Guys. guys. guys! Look! There it is!

735
00:39:02.833 --> 00:39:04.916
And in well under 6 minutes!

736
00:39:11.750 --> 00:39:13.125
The name’s Chloe. right?

737
00:39:14.125 --> 00:39:14.958
Zoe.

738
00:39:15.458 --> 00:39:17.666
Chloe. you and I.
we haven't talked much.

739
00:39:17.750 --> 00:39:20.458
but I think we have quite a lot
in common. Don't you agree?

740
00:39:20.541 --> 00:39:21.750
Um. well...

741
00:39:21.916 --> 00:39:24.125
People like us. we're different.
we have things to do.

742
00:39:24.208 --> 00:39:26.208
we can't spend our lives stuck in here.

743
00:39:26.291 --> 00:39:27.500
But here we are.

744
00:39:27.583 --> 00:39:29.208
Year after year after year.

745
00:39:29.291 --> 00:39:30.541
And why?

746
00:39:30.625 --> 00:39:31.916
Because it's the law?

747
00:39:32.250 --> 00:39:35.250
Exactly. adults and their stupid rules.

748
00:39:35.333 --> 00:39:37.125
Don't they realise
the more rules they make.

749
00:39:37.208 --> 00:39:39.041
the more we want to break them?

750
00:39:39.125 --> 00:39:40.583
That's precisely why I need your help.

751
00:39:40.666 --> 00:39:41.583
Can I count on you?

752
00:39:41.666 --> 00:39:43.250
I guess so. for what?

753
00:39:43.333 --> 00:39:45.208
To steal the exam we have on Monday.

754
00:39:45.541 --> 00:39:46.958
Steal the exam?!

755
00:39:47.041 --> 00:39:50.208
My contact in administration says
Ramirez printed them yesterday.

756
00:39:50.291 --> 00:39:51.583
They're inside his briefcase.

757
00:39:51.666 --> 00:39:53.791
If they catch us.
we’ll get expelled!

758
00:39:53.875 --> 00:39:54.666
Uh-huh.

759
00:39:54.750 --> 00:39:56.291
Whatever happens. we come out ahead.

760
00:39:56.375 --> 00:39:57.208
Don't you love it?

761
00:39:57.750 --> 00:39:59.833
Wow. um... I don't know.

762
00:40:00.166 --> 00:40:01.083
Well I know.

763
00:40:01.166 --> 00:40:03.333
Listen carefully.
I'm not going to repeat this.

764
00:40:03.416 --> 00:40:05.625
I've been working
on a foolproof plan for months.

765
00:40:05.708 --> 00:40:07.875
There's no room for improvisation.
understood?

766
00:40:07.958 --> 00:40:09.916
-Here's what you need to do...
-Hey! Oh my gosh!

767
00:40:10.000 --> 00:40:11.916
A police car just crashed
at the school gate!

768
00:40:12.000 --> 00:40:13.666
What? Another disaster? Run!

769
00:40:16.041 --> 00:40:18.083
Great. what now?

770
00:40:19.791 --> 00:40:22.333
-Now! Go in there and get it!
-What about the plan?

771
00:40:22.416 --> 00:40:24.166
Forget the plan! Move it!

772
00:40:25.166 --> 00:40:26.708
Zoe! Is this later?

773
00:40:26.791 --> 00:40:28.083
Kyle. this isn't a good time!

774
00:40:28.166 --> 00:40:30.583
Oh. sorry!
You want to go check out the car crash?

775
00:40:30.666 --> 00:40:31.458
Come on!

776
00:40:31.541 --> 00:40:34.458
You can sign the form on the way over.
I have a pen here.

777
00:40:34.666 --> 00:40:35.958
No. I'm going to class.

778
00:40:36.041 --> 00:40:37.083
I have to...

779
00:40:37.166 --> 00:40:40.291
Mr. Ramirez asked me
to keep an eye on things while he’s out.

780
00:40:40.666 --> 00:40:42.875
Oh... Someone could break in
and steal something.

781
00:40:42.958 --> 00:40:43.958
that’s good thinking.

782
00:40:44.041 --> 00:40:46.166
Mr. Ramirez is lucky
to have someone like you.

783
00:40:47.000 --> 00:40:48.875
-Like me?
-Yeah. like you.

784
00:40:48.958 --> 00:40:50.125
Someone he can trust.

785
00:41:11.875 --> 00:41:12.958
Zoe!

786
00:41:13.708 --> 00:41:15.125
How did you track me down?

787
00:41:15.291 --> 00:41:16.666
We could smell you
as soon as we got here.

788
00:41:16.750 --> 00:41:18.333
You sweat a lot.
I'd have that checked.

789
00:41:18.500 --> 00:41:20.041
When did you get so good at talking?

790
00:41:20.125 --> 00:41:21.375
About an hour and a half.

791
00:41:21.458 --> 00:41:23.208
We also learned how to use the oven.

792
00:41:23.291 --> 00:41:25.458
tie a bow tie.
turn on the closed captioning.

793
00:41:25.541 --> 00:41:27.666
jump-start a car and driving.

794
00:41:27.750 --> 00:41:29.625
We're trusting our instincts.
that’s all.

795
00:41:29.708 --> 00:41:31.541
Awakening our inner animal.

796
00:41:31.750 --> 00:41:33.166
Defying the status quo.

797
00:41:33.250 --> 00:41:35.083
We're going to Salvatica.
Come with us!

798
00:41:35.250 --> 00:41:37.666
What are you talking about?
You can't be here!

799
00:41:37.958 --> 00:41:38.916
What if someone sees you?

800
00:41:39.000 --> 00:41:40.833
Do you want to get sent to a laboratory?

801
00:41:43.250 --> 00:41:45.250
Well. there was some kind of crash.
or whatever.

802
00:41:45.333 --> 00:41:47.291
What are you asking me for?
I was here...

803
00:41:47.375 --> 00:41:48.458
Gotta go. Later!

804
00:41:54.458 --> 00:41:56.125
No. no. no!

805
00:41:56.750 --> 00:41:59.458
What's going on? The light!
Where's the light?

806
00:41:59.541 --> 00:42:01.833
Please!
I need you to stay there quiet in there!

807
00:42:01.916 --> 00:42:02.916
Come on!

808
00:42:03.000 --> 00:42:04.250
Please. no! The light!

809
00:42:04.333 --> 00:42:06.458
Please. come on! Don't you trust me?

810
00:42:07.541 --> 00:42:08.750
-Yes!
-Yes.

811
00:42:32.500 --> 00:42:33.583
Hey. whatcha doing?

812
00:42:33.666 --> 00:42:35.541
Turning off the sound. just in case.

813
00:42:50.583 --> 00:42:52.916
Don't turn it off!
Someone might need to call us!

814
00:42:53.000 --> 00:42:55.125
Okay. I'll put it on vibrate.

815
00:43:16.833 --> 00:43:18.208
Zoe. what...

816
00:43:18.708 --> 00:43:20.166
What’s going on...?

817
00:43:24.000 --> 00:43:26.375
Zoeee!

818
00:43:29.416 --> 00:43:30.333
No!

819
00:43:30.500 --> 00:43:33.083
The molecular structure
is more complex than I expected.

820
00:43:33.166 --> 00:43:34.875
It's impossible to crack!

821
00:43:34.958 --> 00:43:37.875
Have you considered
inverse fractal decomposition?

822
00:43:38.333 --> 00:43:40.000
Of course! Huh...?

823
00:43:40.375 --> 00:43:41.291
Did you...?

824
00:43:46.000 --> 00:43:47.458
Wait. was that you?

825
00:43:47.666 --> 00:43:48.916
You can talk?

826
00:43:49.250 --> 00:43:52.833
I said... Have you considered
inverse fractal decomposition?

827
00:43:56.125 --> 00:43:57.208
Oh my word!

828
00:43:57.375 --> 00:43:59.708
The mixture of the compound
and the energy drink...

829
00:43:59.791 --> 00:44:01.458
...has accelerated our evolution.

830
00:44:01.625 --> 00:44:04.416
It's a little bit more complex
than that. but well deduced.

831
00:44:04.750 --> 00:44:06.666
This proves my theory is correct.

832
00:44:07.333 --> 00:44:09.875
The berries alter
the DNA of the animals!

833
00:44:09.958 --> 00:44:12.458
Did you hear that. Robert?
My theory is correct!

834
00:44:12.541 --> 00:44:13.583
Woo-hooo!

835
00:44:14.958 --> 00:44:18.083
Reverse fractal decomposition.
here we go.

836
00:44:19.416 --> 00:44:21.416
Utilizing the endoplasmic reticulum?

837
00:44:22.083 --> 00:44:23.083
What else?

838
00:44:23.166 --> 00:44:25.541
Finally. someone who
knows what I'm talking about.

839
00:44:27.958 --> 00:44:28.958
Not now!

840
00:44:31.916 --> 00:44:32.916
What did she do?

841
00:44:33.458 --> 00:44:34.500
Expelled!

842
00:44:34.583 --> 00:44:36.208
For stealing an exam!

843
00:44:36.375 --> 00:44:38.625
What am I going to do?
Do you know how bad this is for me?

844
00:44:38.708 --> 00:44:39.666
The mean lady!

845
00:44:39.750 --> 00:44:40.791
-What do we do?
-Shhh.

846
00:44:40.875 --> 00:44:42.791
Mom. There’s something you need to know.

847
00:44:42.875 --> 00:44:44.000
I don't want to hear a word!

848
00:44:44.083 --> 00:44:45.875
I hope you enjoyed
your last day of freedom

849
00:44:45.958 --> 00:44:47.791
because you're going to spend
the rest of your high school days

850
00:44:47.875 --> 00:44:49.666
locked up in boarding school.

851
00:44:54.958 --> 00:44:57.500
I hope it's important
because I'm in big trouble...

852
00:44:57.666 --> 00:44:59.458
Your daughter stole an exam!

853
00:44:59.541 --> 00:45:01.625
Zoe. how could you let them catch you?

854
00:45:01.708 --> 00:45:02.875
-Dad...
-That's just great.

855
00:45:03.041 --> 00:45:05.583
This is your fault for raising her
to believe in the law of least effort!

856
00:45:05.666 --> 00:45:06.833
-Mom...
-What do you mean my fault?

857
00:45:06.916 --> 00:45:09.375
How can it be all my fault
when I hardly ever see her?

858
00:45:09.458 --> 00:45:10.625
Oh. you’ll see her plenty.

859
00:45:10.708 --> 00:45:12.791
She'll stay with you
until she goes to boarding school.

860
00:45:12.875 --> 00:45:15.708
What? No. no. no. no.
that's terrible for me.

861
00:45:15.791 --> 00:45:17.041
It would be worse for me.

862
00:45:17.791 --> 00:45:19.250
-Heads.
-Tails.

863
00:45:23.458 --> 00:45:25.250
Zoe. stop that nonsense right now!

864
00:45:27.166 --> 00:45:28.625
Is this normal for her?

865
00:45:29.041 --> 00:45:30.750
Zoe! I said to stop that!

866
00:45:30.833 --> 00:45:32.958
Woah. everything's under control here!

867
00:45:33.041 --> 00:45:35.500
Please forgive our friend.
she's a wee bit nervous.

868
00:45:35.583 --> 00:45:36.916
Don’t worry. we were just going...

869
00:45:38.750 --> 00:45:41.500
Did your rabbit just talk.
or am I going nuts?

870
00:45:41.583 --> 00:45:42.833
Oh my word!

871
00:45:42.916 --> 00:45:45.416
You went into my laboratory. didn’t you?

872
00:45:49.083 --> 00:45:49.916
I'm not angry.

873
00:45:50.000 --> 00:45:51.875
I just want to know
if you ate any of the berries

874
00:45:51.958 --> 00:45:54.166
they brought me from the Arctic.
that's all.

875
00:45:54.250 --> 00:45:56.666
Well. maybe one or two?

876
00:45:57.458 --> 00:45:58.875
Zoe. this is...

877
00:45:59.875 --> 00:46:01.500
Fascinating!

878
00:46:01.583 --> 00:46:04.041
You intertwined your genetic memories!

879
00:46:04.375 --> 00:46:05.208
How did it happen?

880
00:46:05.291 --> 00:46:07.250
Through direct contact?
Indirect contact?

881
00:46:07.416 --> 00:46:08.583
Before or after ingestion?

882
00:46:08.666 --> 00:46:10.166
Did you notice anything unusual?

883
00:46:10.250 --> 00:46:11.875
Sensations. sounds?
Any strange lumps?

884
00:46:11.958 --> 00:46:13.541
Dad! Say something to her!

885
00:46:28.458 --> 00:46:30.375
This exceeds all my expectations!

886
00:46:30.458 --> 00:46:32.500
We’ll grab those cuties
and get back to the lab.

887
00:46:32.583 --> 00:46:34.583
-So many tests to carry out.
-No way!

888
00:46:34.666 --> 00:46:37.000
What kind of mother
experiments on their own daughter?

889
00:46:37.083 --> 00:46:39.875
-Are you implying I'm a bad mother?
-Bad? You're dangerous!

890
00:46:39.958 --> 00:46:42.708
-Let her go. she's coming with me!
-No. she's not!

891
00:46:42.791 --> 00:46:43.833
Ah!

892
00:46:45.083 --> 00:46:46.166
Stop! You’ll hurt her!

893
00:46:46.250 --> 00:46:48.708
There must be
a civilized way to do this?

894
00:46:48.791 --> 00:46:50.333
You know. the monkey's right.

895
00:46:50.416 --> 00:46:51.250
Heads!

896
00:46:52.833 --> 00:46:54.125
What? No!

897
00:47:07.208 --> 00:47:08.291
Gordon!

898
00:47:11.750 --> 00:47:12.958
What are we doing here?

899
00:47:13.041 --> 00:47:15.041
I want to introduce you
to someone.

900
00:47:19.583 --> 00:47:20.500
Yeah. well?

901
00:47:20.583 --> 00:47:23.416
Come on. say something.
don't be rude.

902
00:47:23.750 --> 00:47:26.791
Is there anything to eat here or what?
I'm starving. Is it just me?

903
00:47:26.875 --> 00:47:28.000
What's the Wi-Fi’s password?

904
00:47:28.083 --> 00:47:29.291
Are we going to be here long?

905
00:47:29.375 --> 00:47:31.250
If we are.
I’d love to take my shoes off.

906
00:47:33.000 --> 00:47:34.291
Oh my goodness!

907
00:47:34.791 --> 00:47:36.083
We’ll get you a menu right away.

908
00:47:36.291 --> 00:47:37.958
VivaPiñata_99.

909
00:47:38.041 --> 00:47:39.791
And you. make yourself at home.

910
00:47:39.875 --> 00:47:41.125
And you are?

911
00:47:43.500 --> 00:47:45.375
I’m someone that weird stuff happens to.

912
00:47:45.458 --> 00:47:46.583
It’s incredible!

913
00:47:46.666 --> 00:47:48.625
You're incredible. too!

914
00:47:48.875 --> 00:47:50.500
What an exotic little group.

915
00:47:50.666 --> 00:47:52.250
Did you know that the wombat

916
00:47:52.333 --> 00:47:54.916
is the only animal in the world
that poops square poop?

917
00:47:55.083 --> 00:47:56.500
-Oh. well.
-Oh boy. do we ever.

918
00:47:56.583 --> 00:47:58.000
That makes them easy to stack.

919
00:47:58.083 --> 00:48:01.083
Gordon. do you think I could
talk to you for just a moment?

920
00:48:01.250 --> 00:48:04.333
Guys. if you want. you can wait
over here inside the break room.

921
00:48:05.208 --> 00:48:08.125
Are we really going to spend
Friday in an office?

922
00:48:08.208 --> 00:48:09.666
The most bori...

923
00:48:09.750 --> 00:48:12.041
...coolest place in the world!

924
00:48:12.125 --> 00:48:13.708
Maybe we can wait a little while...

925
00:48:14.375 --> 00:48:16.000
You're a genius. Gordon!

926
00:48:16.083 --> 00:48:17.833
I knew that I could count on you.

927
00:48:17.916 --> 00:48:21.166
Your daughter and her pets have had
their genetic memories intertwined.

928
00:48:21.250 --> 00:48:22.291
Right? Am I right?

929
00:48:22.458 --> 00:48:23.958
Yeah. something like that. y’know?

930
00:48:24.041 --> 00:48:24.875
How did you do it?

931
00:48:24.958 --> 00:48:27.166
With an ultra-complex
mutagenic conglomerate

932
00:48:27.333 --> 00:48:30.583
that acts on genomes by altering
their cellular structure. right?

933
00:48:30.666 --> 00:48:33.500
It's a complicated process.

934
00:48:33.583 --> 00:48:35.375
I don't want to bore you with details.

935
00:48:35.458 --> 00:48:37.916
Talking animals. yeah?

936
00:48:38.416 --> 00:48:40.583
We're going to make a fortune.

937
00:48:40.750 --> 00:48:42.500
Great idea. Talking pets!

938
00:48:43.041 --> 00:48:43.958
That’s super.

939
00:48:44.041 --> 00:48:44.916
Leave them here.

940
00:48:45.000 --> 00:48:47.458
we'll take care of the marketing
and everything.

941
00:48:47.625 --> 00:48:48.875
Yeah. we’ll leave them.

942
00:48:48.958 --> 00:48:51.250
Wait.
I should to talk to Zoe about that.

943
00:48:51.333 --> 00:48:52.458
She can stay as well!

944
00:48:52.541 --> 00:48:54.083
We’ve got plenty of room.

945
00:48:54.166 --> 00:48:56.166
Our company is one big happy family.

946
00:48:56.250 --> 00:48:57.166
Then I should stay too?

947
00:48:57.250 --> 00:48:59.791
No. you go home and rest until tomorrow.

948
00:48:59.875 --> 00:49:00.958
You've earned it.

949
00:49:01.041 --> 00:49:03.166
You must be exhausted
after all that effort.

950
00:49:03.250 --> 00:49:04.541
Well. a little. yes.

951
00:49:04.916 --> 00:49:07.166
But I still need to talk to Zoe...

952
00:49:10.791 --> 00:49:13.583
I really do try my best.
but it’s just so hard. you know?

953
00:49:14.166 --> 00:49:15.166
Am I a bad mother?

954
00:49:15.250 --> 00:49:16.666
Why exactly?

955
00:49:16.750 --> 00:49:19.208
Because I have to pay more attention
to my work than to my daughter?

956
00:49:19.833 --> 00:49:21.875
I don't know.
Do you do that?

957
00:49:22.875 --> 00:49:23.791
I don't know. do I?

958
00:49:23.958 --> 00:49:25.000
I do!

959
00:49:25.833 --> 00:49:26.750
Oh I do!

960
00:49:26.833 --> 00:49:28.333
I'm a terrible mother!

961
00:49:30.291 --> 00:49:31.291
The analysis!

962
00:49:34.916 --> 00:49:37.958
It seems the compound
is more invasive than we had thought.

963
00:49:38.625 --> 00:49:39.458
Oh no.

964
00:49:39.708 --> 00:49:42.916
that means soon Zoe
will turn into an animal forever!

965
00:49:46.750 --> 00:49:48.000
Unless...

966
00:49:48.458 --> 00:49:50.125
Unless we find the antidote!

967
00:49:50.208 --> 00:49:52.833
I may be a bad mother.
but I'm a great scientist.

968
00:49:52.916 --> 00:49:54.041
Let's get to work!

969
00:49:54.833 --> 00:49:55.750
One.

970
00:49:56.083 --> 00:49:56.916
two.

971
00:49:57.291 --> 00:50:00.250
three pizzas for free.99!

972
00:50:01.958 --> 00:50:03.333
This place is high tech.

973
00:50:03.416 --> 00:50:06.083
But the sofas are like
something from grandma's house.

974
00:50:08.000 --> 00:50:09.958
Okay. grandma from the future!

975
00:50:10.416 --> 00:50:11.791
How about a little snack?

976
00:50:12.750 --> 00:50:13.500
Hey!

977
00:50:13.666 --> 00:50:15.000
You wanted a snack. didn't you?

978
00:50:15.083 --> 00:50:16.000
Well. snack up!

979
00:50:16.583 --> 00:50:19.041
Wow! And I thought reality was wild.

980
00:50:54.708 --> 00:50:56.625
Wow! Can you do that again?

981
00:50:56.791 --> 00:50:57.750
Do what?

982
00:50:59.083 --> 00:51:00.625
Ugh. Where's my dad?

983
00:51:01.416 --> 00:51:04.000
He left. he had things to do.
Want a smoothie?

984
00:51:04.083 --> 00:51:05.000
No. Great.

985
00:51:05.083 --> 00:51:07.291
Abandoned with strangers.
Again.

986
00:51:07.666 --> 00:51:10.208
What do you mean stranger?
I'm TJ Johnson!

987
00:51:10.291 --> 00:51:13.208
Scientist. philanthropist. influencer.

988
00:51:13.291 --> 00:51:15.375
Kids these days
aren’t in touch with the world.

989
00:51:16.083 --> 00:51:18.166
Suzie. look up TJ Johnson.

990
00:51:18.250 --> 00:51:21.000
Showing results for TJ Johnson.

991
00:51:21.416 --> 00:51:24.166
TJ Johnson.
a selfless and generous leader.

992
00:51:24.250 --> 00:51:26.041
...as concerned about the planet
as TJ Johnson.

993
00:51:26.125 --> 00:51:28.583
When TJ Johnson's peace speech
brought tears to the eyes of...

994
00:51:28.666 --> 00:51:29.750
-TJ Johnson.
-TJ Johnson.

995
00:51:29.833 --> 00:51:32.125
I'm more into kitten videos.
Meow!

996
00:51:32.208 --> 00:51:34.791
And speaking of animals.
my DNA is having a party

997
00:51:34.875 --> 00:51:37.208
and I don't know how long
I'll be able to control it.

998
00:51:38.250 --> 00:51:39.916
Why is it something you want to control?

999
00:51:40.000 --> 00:51:42.708
What's happening to you
is called genetic mutation.

1000
00:51:42.791 --> 00:51:44.166
It means you're evolving.

1001
00:51:44.250 --> 00:51:46.625
It means you’re becoming
something unique.

1002
00:51:46.708 --> 00:51:48.666
I wish my parents thought like you.

1003
00:51:48.750 --> 00:51:50.791
They want to send me to boarding school.

1004
00:51:51.083 --> 00:51:53.041
Oh. I went to boarding school too.

1005
00:51:53.541 --> 00:51:55.208
Really? How was it?

1006
00:51:55.375 --> 00:51:56.875
It was horrible and traumatic.

1007
00:51:57.000 --> 00:51:57.958
but fine.

1008
00:51:58.041 --> 00:51:59.458
Got time for a flashback?

1009
00:51:59.541 --> 00:52:00.708
Hmm... Okay.

1010
00:52:01.875 --> 00:52:04.708
I'll never forget the day I got there.

1011
00:52:04.958 --> 00:52:07.750
My parents told me
we were going to buy yogurt.

1012
00:52:07.916 --> 00:52:09.208
but that was a lie.

1013
00:52:09.583 --> 00:52:12.208
Nobody has to packs their bags
to buy yogurt.

1014
00:52:12.458 --> 00:52:15.416
I was only 8 years old.
and already alone.

1015
00:52:15.583 --> 00:52:17.875
I tried to make friends
the only way I knew how:

1016
00:52:18.041 --> 00:52:20.541
by proving that
I was smarter than all of them.

1017
00:52:20.875 --> 00:52:22.833
But for some reason it didn't work.

1018
00:52:23.125 --> 00:52:25.000
I got used to the loneliness

1019
00:52:25.083 --> 00:52:28.333
and devoted myself
to more useful things than having fun.

1020
00:52:28.416 --> 00:52:31.791
I discovered my true passion: science.

1021
00:52:31.958 --> 00:52:34.125
I began to search
for the origin of life.

1022
00:52:34.375 --> 00:52:37.541
The spark that transforms
something small and fragile

1023
00:52:37.625 --> 00:52:39.916
into something big and powerful.

1024
00:52:40.000 --> 00:52:43.916
How life finds ways to thrive
under any circumstance.

1025
00:52:45.250 --> 00:52:46.708
No. no!

1026
00:52:51.916 --> 00:52:56.541
But the world wasn't made for curious.
sensitive people like me.

1027
00:52:56.916 --> 00:52:59.625
The world belonged to the strongest.

1028
00:53:07.875 --> 00:53:09.583
So I turned away from everything

1029
00:53:09.666 --> 00:53:11.625
and studied like no one else.

1030
00:53:11.708 --> 00:53:12.791
Waiting for bad weather

1031
00:53:12.875 --> 00:53:15.333
to make my oath as epic as possible.

1032
00:53:16.416 --> 00:53:18.458
and when that storm arrived...

1033
00:53:18.541 --> 00:53:21.291
I swore I would change everything.

1034
00:53:21.375 --> 00:53:23.916
I would become so strong that one day

1035
00:53:24.000 --> 00:53:25.791
I would rule the world!

1036
00:53:27.541 --> 00:53:30.000
That is. figuratively speaking.
of course.

1037
00:53:31.458 --> 00:53:33.583
I gotta go. but just so you know.

1038
00:53:33.666 --> 00:53:34.875
this isn't a boarding school.

1039
00:53:34.958 --> 00:53:37.000
here you can do anything you desire.

1040
00:53:37.083 --> 00:53:38.333
So. what are you gonna do?

1041
00:53:45.083 --> 00:53:47.500
Test 6007. loading simulation!

1042
00:53:47.583 --> 00:53:50.583
I have a good feeling about this.
I think this’ll be the one.

1043
00:54:08.041 --> 00:54:10.708
Aaaah! You animal!

1044
00:54:15.625 --> 00:54:16.750
What's going on here?

1045
00:54:16.833 --> 00:54:18.333
She tried to bite me!

1046
00:54:19.125 --> 00:54:21.625
What are you doing there?
That lamp cost a fortune...

1047
00:54:21.708 --> 00:54:22.666
Get down here right now!

1048
00:54:27.333 --> 00:54:30.000
That's no way to treat
designer furniture. Zoe!

1049
00:54:30.083 --> 00:54:31.375
I'm talking to you!

1050
00:54:32.416 --> 00:54:33.833
Look at the mess you’ve made!

1051
00:54:41.708 --> 00:54:43.958
Don't you growl at me. young lady!

1052
00:54:44.166 --> 00:54:45.375
Zoe. come!

1053
00:54:45.791 --> 00:54:47.916
Keep an eye on her. I'll be right back!

1054
00:54:57.625 --> 00:54:59.041
This is Peggy. If you're hearing this.

1055
00:54:59.125 --> 00:55:00.875
I'm not interested
in what you have to say.

1056
00:55:00.958 --> 00:55:02.291
Gordon! You're back.

1057
00:55:02.375 --> 00:55:04.208
What are you doing here?
Everything okay?

1058
00:55:04.500 --> 00:55:07.583
Zoe's a little genetically confused.

1059
00:55:07.958 --> 00:55:10.875
I think we should talk to her mother.
she understands this stuff.

1060
00:55:10.958 --> 00:55:12.333
What? No!

1061
00:55:12.416 --> 00:55:13.333
She's just a kid!

1062
00:55:13.416 --> 00:55:15.125
She's having some fun.

1063
00:55:15.458 --> 00:55:16.791
Relax Gordon.

1064
00:55:17.916 --> 00:55:19.166
And let us do our work.

1065
00:55:34.375 --> 00:55:35.458
What is all this?

1066
00:55:35.833 --> 00:55:37.416
Gordon. what did I just tell you?

1067
00:55:37.500 --> 00:55:38.916
This is a top-secret project.

1068
00:55:39.000 --> 00:55:41.041
you have no business being in here.

1069
00:55:41.125 --> 00:55:42.666
You're spying on my daughter!

1070
00:55:42.750 --> 00:55:45.375
We are studying
your daughter’s behaviour.

1071
00:55:45.458 --> 00:55:47.000
But why?

1072
00:55:47.291 --> 00:55:48.000
But why?

1073
00:55:48.375 --> 00:55:50.541
To find out what's going on
inside of her.

1074
00:55:50.625 --> 00:55:52.958
turn it into a delicious
vanilla-flavored powder

1075
00:55:53.041 --> 00:55:54.041
and sell it!

1076
00:55:54.125 --> 00:55:55.125
Just look at her!

1077
00:55:55.375 --> 00:55:57.250
Strength. agility. instinct...

1078
00:55:57.333 --> 00:56:01.375
All the qualities of the animal world
will be available to anyone.

1079
00:56:01.458 --> 00:56:02.500
This. Gordon.

1080
00:56:03.000 --> 00:56:04.208
this is the next step

1081
00:56:04.291 --> 00:56:06.125
in the evolution of humanity.

1082
00:56:06.291 --> 00:56:08.125
We didn't agree to any of this at all.

1083
00:56:08.333 --> 00:56:10.000
We're getting out of here right now.

1084
00:56:10.958 --> 00:56:13.250
Gordon. Zoe is not in danger.

1085
00:56:13.333 --> 00:56:15.125
I'm a scientist. not a...

1086
00:56:15.208 --> 00:56:17.375
Why am I wasting my time
explaining this?

1087
00:56:17.458 --> 00:56:18.583
Security!

1088
00:56:18.666 --> 00:56:20.416
Detain Gordon Frink!

1089
00:56:23.625 --> 00:56:25.250
No! Back! Sit!

1090
00:56:25.333 --> 00:56:26.416
I said. sit!

1091
00:56:27.500 --> 00:56:28.625
Blinky! Womby!

1092
00:56:28.708 --> 00:56:29.458
A little help here!

1093
00:56:29.625 --> 00:56:31.625
I'm trying to listen to an audiobook.

1094
00:56:31.708 --> 00:56:32.833
if you don't mind.

1095
00:56:33.000 --> 00:56:34.708
We have to do something!

1096
00:56:34.791 --> 00:56:36.291
This has gotten way out of hand!

1097
00:56:36.375 --> 00:56:38.083
Leave her alone. she's just playing.

1098
00:56:38.166 --> 00:56:39.791
She’s just playing?

1099
00:56:41.500 --> 00:56:44.333
That’s just great. perfect. wonderful.

1100
00:56:44.416 --> 00:56:46.833
My personal best
and I didn't get the statement!

1101
00:56:47.500 --> 00:56:49.458
No! No! Get down!

1102
00:56:49.541 --> 00:56:51.041
Bad human! Bad!

1103
00:56:51.208 --> 00:56:54.125
Leave her alone.
she's just playing with you.

1104
00:56:56.250 --> 00:56:58.083
We're getting out of here right now!

1105
00:56:59.041 --> 00:57:00.250
It's about time.

1106
00:57:00.333 --> 00:57:01.958
Hey. get back here!

1107
00:57:05.458 --> 00:57:06.500
Ow!

1108
00:57:08.041 --> 00:57:09.041
Zoe!

1109
00:57:24.250 --> 00:57:25.416
No!

1110
00:57:28.666 --> 00:57:29.666
Now what?

1111
00:57:30.708 --> 00:57:31.916
What are you doing?

1112
00:57:32.000 --> 00:57:33.750
Have you ever heard of due process?

1113
00:57:33.833 --> 00:57:35.500
What's this? What's going on?

1114
00:57:35.583 --> 00:57:37.250
Let us go. bearded man!

1115
00:57:37.333 --> 00:57:39.250
-We thought you were chill!
-I am!

1116
00:57:39.416 --> 00:57:42.125
If you were.
you'd respect our personal space!

1117
00:57:42.208 --> 00:57:43.666
Will you two zip it?

1118
00:57:44.750 --> 00:57:45.583
There they are!

1119
00:57:51.708 --> 00:57:54.166
I was just on my way to the bathroom.
Is it a bad time?

1120
00:57:54.250 --> 00:57:55.291
Out of the way!

1121
00:57:57.833 --> 00:58:00.333
Stuffed animal transport coordinator
coming through!

1122
00:58:00.416 --> 00:58:03.000
That's not the
stuffed animal transport coordinator!

1123
00:58:03.166 --> 00:58:05.791
Open the door!
Open the door now!

1124
00:58:05.875 --> 00:58:07.875
That is not the real head of security!

1125
00:58:07.958 --> 00:58:09.416
Do not open the door!

1126
00:58:09.916 --> 00:58:12.250
Look. you guys figure it out
among yourselves.

1127
00:58:12.458 --> 00:58:14.250
Horrible! Horrible!

1128
00:58:14.333 --> 00:58:17.166
I haven't felt so humiliated
in my three years of life!

1129
00:58:17.250 --> 00:58:19.125
I hope you have a good lawyer!

1130
00:58:19.208 --> 00:58:20.458
So that's it?

1131
00:58:20.625 --> 00:58:22.125
The kidnapping is over?

1132
00:58:22.416 --> 00:58:23.833
I'm not kidnapping you.

1133
00:58:23.916 --> 00:58:25.333
I'm saving you!

1134
00:58:25.416 --> 00:58:27.416
Saving us? Saving us from what?

1135
00:58:28.333 --> 00:58:29.625
What is this place?

1136
00:58:30.041 --> 00:58:31.166
What’s with all these...

1137
00:58:31.250 --> 00:58:32.666
Cages. cages!

1138
00:58:38.583 --> 00:58:40.833
Is this what I think it is...?

1139
00:58:51.666 --> 00:58:53.833
Oh no! What have I done now?

1140
00:58:55.458 --> 00:58:56.541
Ah!

1141
00:58:57.125 --> 00:58:58.083
No!

1142
00:59:02.333 --> 00:59:03.791
Guys? Hello?

1143
00:59:05.958 --> 00:59:08.875
I'm the guy with the beard.
why aren't you insulting me anymore?

1144
00:59:08.958 --> 00:59:11.375
Gordon. Gordon. Gordon...

1145
00:59:11.916 --> 00:59:14.791
Everything was going fine
until you stuck your nose in it.

1146
00:59:14.875 --> 00:59:17.541
Just wait until people find out
you're experimenting on animals!

1147
00:59:17.625 --> 00:59:20.875
The thing is. Gordon
as long as they don't see it.

1148
00:59:20.958 --> 00:59:22.250
people don't care.

1149
00:59:22.458 --> 00:59:23.458
Now get him!

1150
00:59:30.500 --> 00:59:31.458
Come on. guys!

1151
00:59:31.541 --> 00:59:33.166
The power's out. whop-dee-doo.

1152
00:59:33.250 --> 00:59:34.541
Big problem. huh?

1153
00:59:38.916 --> 00:59:41.083
Okay. now that is a big problem. yeah.

1154
00:59:47.125 --> 00:59:49.583
Gordon! You are fired!

1155
00:59:49.875 --> 00:59:50.958
Fine with me!

1156
00:59:59.166 --> 01:00:00.708
Peggy. I've lost Zoe!

1157
01:00:00.791 --> 01:00:03.958
I left her at my office. it was easier
for someone else to take care of her

1158
01:00:04.041 --> 01:00:06.000
and then she went wild.
and then she bit me

1159
01:00:06.083 --> 01:00:07.125
and then she ran away.

1160
01:00:07.208 --> 01:00:09.000
And now I don't even know
where she could be.

1161
01:00:09.083 --> 01:00:12.250
what her favourite spots are.
I don't even know who her friends are...

1162
01:00:12.541 --> 01:00:15.000
I don't even have a recent photo
to show the police!

1163
01:00:15.083 --> 01:00:16.666
I'm a terrible father!

1164
01:00:19.333 --> 01:00:20.375
Come on in.

1165
01:00:21.541 --> 01:00:23.875
A little while ago
I heard a noise and found her in here.

1166
01:00:25.833 --> 01:00:27.416
I haven't been able to get her out.

1167
01:00:28.375 --> 01:00:29.416
What's wrong with her?

1168
01:00:29.583 --> 01:00:31.333
The mutation has taken control of her.

1169
01:00:31.416 --> 01:00:33.916
In less than an hour. she'll lose
what little humanity she has left.

1170
01:00:34.000 --> 01:00:36.208
Oh. no.
I can’t believe I let this happen.

1171
01:00:36.375 --> 01:00:37.625
You let it happen. Gordon?

1172
01:00:37.708 --> 01:00:38.875
I caused it all.

1173
01:00:38.958 --> 01:00:40.666
Peggy. this is all my fault.

1174
01:00:40.833 --> 01:00:43.250
No. Gordon.
If anyone is to blame. I am.

1175
01:00:43.333 --> 01:00:46.291
-No. I'm the one to blame.
-I'm much to blame than you are here...

1176
01:00:54.541 --> 01:00:57.125
-Zoe. we're such terrible parents.
-Zoe. we're such terrible parents.

1177
01:00:57.208 --> 01:00:58.958
-Please forgive us.
-Please forgive us.

1178
01:01:13.916 --> 01:01:14.875
Huh?

1179
01:01:16.500 --> 01:01:18.583
Why are they back to normal?
No idea.

1180
01:01:18.750 --> 01:01:21.458
They changed when they saw
what was happening in the lab.

1181
01:01:21.541 --> 01:01:22.916
It had to be the fright of their lives.

1182
01:01:25.000 --> 01:01:26.125
A fright...

1183
01:01:26.541 --> 01:01:27.500
I got it!

1184
01:01:38.458 --> 01:01:40.208
Adrenaline! It’s adrenaline!

1185
01:01:40.916 --> 01:01:42.250
Yes. of course!

1186
01:01:48.708 --> 01:01:49.750
Huh?

1187
01:01:50.208 --> 01:01:52.666
Oh. mice of the future.
that’s great.

1188
01:01:52.750 --> 01:01:53.791
Have you come up with anything?

1189
01:01:53.958 --> 01:01:56.333
When they got frightened.
the animals secreted adrenaline!

1190
01:01:56.416 --> 01:01:59.125
And that’s the key we needed
to find to unlock the antidote!

1191
01:01:59.208 --> 01:02:00.791
We can save Zoe!

1192
01:02:37.416 --> 01:02:38.750
Yeah!

1193
01:02:46.208 --> 01:02:48.375
It’s okay. Don't worry. honey.

1194
01:02:48.458 --> 01:02:49.500
It won’t hurt a bit.

1195
01:02:49.583 --> 01:02:51.625
Hello. friends!
Today we're going to explore...

1196
01:02:51.708 --> 01:02:53.083
Works every single time.

1197
01:02:53.166 --> 01:02:55.291
the uncertainty principle.

1198
01:02:55.375 --> 01:02:57.583
A consequence of quantum formalism...

1199
01:02:58.083 --> 01:02:59.208
Hey!

1200
01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:01.041
Ouch. Mom!

1201
01:03:01.125 --> 01:03:02.833
What? It was the antidote!

1202
01:03:02.916 --> 01:03:05.583
And it had to be an injection.
it couldn't be a syrup.

1203
01:03:05.750 --> 01:03:07.791
How about thanks and a big hug.
you two?

1204
01:03:09.750 --> 01:03:10.708
Thanks.

1205
01:03:12.333 --> 01:03:13.875
Sorry to interrupt.

1206
01:03:14.333 --> 01:03:16.000
We have reached 3 conclusions.

1207
01:03:16.083 --> 01:03:19.458
One: this compound is the origin
of life on Earth.

1208
01:03:19.541 --> 01:03:21.333
Two: it is extremely fragile.

1209
01:03:21.416 --> 01:03:22.708
so revealing its source

1210
01:03:22.875 --> 01:03:25.875
would put the planet in a situation
we have called...

1211
01:03:25.958 --> 01:03:26.916
Boom!

1212
01:03:27.833 --> 01:03:28.750
And three:

1213
01:03:28.833 --> 01:03:31.416
as a civilization you are a disaster.

1214
01:03:31.500 --> 01:03:33.125
so. wishing you the best.

1215
01:03:33.291 --> 01:03:34.875
we're going as far away as possible.

1216
01:03:35.500 --> 01:03:37.500
Goodbye. humans!

1217
01:03:38.916 --> 01:03:40.666
He can’t be serious. can he?

1218
01:03:42.750 --> 01:03:44.791
Well. well. well...

1219
01:03:44.958 --> 01:03:46.500
How interesting!

1220
01:03:46.583 --> 01:03:48.958
That’s just the information
that I’m looking for.

1221
01:03:49.250 --> 01:03:51.125
Mom. Dad. what's going on?

1222
01:03:51.208 --> 01:03:53.375
Zoe. grab your pets.
and get out of here!

1223
01:03:53.708 --> 01:03:54.666
What? Why?

1224
01:03:54.750 --> 01:03:56.208
Because he wants to puree them!

1225
01:03:56.291 --> 01:03:57.666
-Run!
-Hey!

1226
01:03:58.875 --> 01:03:59.875
Hey!

1227
01:04:01.208 --> 01:04:02.291
You stay away from her!

1228
01:04:02.375 --> 01:04:03.625
Get out of our house!

1229
01:04:04.708 --> 01:04:06.458
Oh yes. yes...

1230
01:04:06.541 --> 01:04:10.083
What you’ve got here
is very interesting...

1231
01:04:11.791 --> 01:04:12.875
No.

1232
01:04:13.541 --> 01:04:14.916
Is this...

1233
01:04:15.083 --> 01:04:18.291
The ultra-complex mutagenic conglomerate

1234
01:04:18.375 --> 01:04:20.916
that acts upon genomes by actually

1235
01:04:21.000 --> 01:04:23.416
altering their cellular structure.

1236
01:04:23.583 --> 01:04:24.541
No. no. no.

1237
01:04:25.083 --> 01:04:26.708
It's the motherlode!

1238
01:04:27.125 --> 01:04:29.583
The secret to all-powerful DNA.

1239
01:04:29.666 --> 01:04:30.875
supreme life energy.

1240
01:04:31.041 --> 01:04:32.166
the power of a god.

1241
01:04:32.250 --> 01:04:34.250
superanimals. superhumans.

1242
01:04:34.333 --> 01:04:35.333
superarmies.

1243
01:04:35.416 --> 01:04:36.875
president of the world.

1244
01:04:37.041 --> 01:04:38.833
person of the year!

1245
01:04:40.125 --> 01:04:41.208
In the Arctic?

1246
01:04:41.791 --> 01:04:43.041
Could it be?

1247
01:04:43.458 --> 01:04:45.125
Yes! It's real!

1248
01:04:45.208 --> 01:04:46.333
It's real!

1249
01:04:48.000 --> 01:04:49.083
Here it is!

1250
01:04:49.166 --> 01:04:52.166
I found the spark of life
after looking for so long!

1251
01:04:53.500 --> 01:04:55.250
Yeah. you found it.
What a creep.

1252
01:05:04.833 --> 01:05:07.375
An Exploratron X-99?

1253
01:05:07.458 --> 01:05:09.291
I loved those when I was a boy.

1254
01:05:09.375 --> 01:05:10.416
And do you know why?

1255
01:05:15.291 --> 01:05:16.833
Because they were so basic.

1256
01:05:17.000 --> 01:05:18.375
Arctic here I come!

1257
01:05:18.458 --> 01:05:20.291
These two know more
than they're letting on.

1258
01:05:20.375 --> 01:05:22.458
-so we're taking them with us.
-Don’t touch me!

1259
01:05:23.916 --> 01:05:24.875
Bye. bye...

1260
01:05:24.958 --> 01:05:27.000
Don't do this. man.
we're friends. aren’t we?

1261
01:05:27.083 --> 01:05:28.250
Your name's Gary. isn’t it?

1262
01:05:28.333 --> 01:05:29.458
No? It’s not?

1263
01:05:29.541 --> 01:05:31.333
Then who is Gary? Is he Gary?

1264
01:05:31.875 --> 01:05:33.625
-What about her?
-Leave her here.

1265
01:05:33.708 --> 01:05:35.666
There’s nothing special
about her anymore.

1266
01:05:35.750 --> 01:05:37.250
No! Let them go!

1267
01:05:39.416 --> 01:05:40.375
Go away. brat.

1268
01:05:47.333 --> 01:05:48.916
Oh no. Oh no.

1269
01:05:49.708 --> 01:05:50.541
Oh. no!

1270
01:05:58.083 --> 01:05:59.291
Is anyone here?

1271
01:06:01.208 --> 01:06:02.583
If anyone is here.

1272
01:06:03.416 --> 01:06:06.541
please know that I am very nervous
and I am not responsible for my actions.

1273
01:06:06.625 --> 01:06:07.708
Hey. what’s up?

1274
01:06:08.250 --> 01:06:09.416
Oh. no. Zoe!

1275
01:06:09.625 --> 01:06:11.458
I broke your lamp!
I'm so sorry.

1276
01:06:11.541 --> 01:06:13.458
My head is like a rock.
medical condition.

1277
01:06:13.625 --> 01:06:14.416
How did you get in?

1278
01:06:14.583 --> 01:06:15.916
Front door was open.

1279
01:06:16.000 --> 01:06:17.833
I’ve got your volunteer form right here.

1280
01:06:19.916 --> 01:06:20.833
What?

1281
01:06:22.041 --> 01:06:23.458
There! You happy?

1282
01:06:24.416 --> 01:06:26.333
I guess so... yeah.

1283
01:06:26.541 --> 01:06:28.208
It's a strange feeling.

1284
01:06:28.291 --> 01:06:29.791
no one has ever signed one.

1285
01:06:30.750 --> 01:06:31.875
Is everything okay?

1286
01:06:31.958 --> 01:06:33.208
Nothing's okay.

1287
01:06:34.208 --> 01:06:35.250
Anything I can do?

1288
01:06:35.333 --> 01:06:36.250
I don't know. Kyle.

1289
01:06:36.333 --> 01:06:38.250
A tech guru has kidnapped my parents

1290
01:06:38.416 --> 01:06:39.625
and taken them to the Arctic

1291
01:06:39.708 --> 01:06:42.333
in search of the mutagenic fruits
of an alien plant.

1292
01:06:42.583 --> 01:06:44.166
So you tell me what you can do.

1293
01:06:44.625 --> 01:06:46.541
Never mind. it's all my fault.

1294
01:06:46.625 --> 01:06:47.541
I've done it.

1295
01:06:47.625 --> 01:06:49.833
I've messed up so badly
that I'm all alone.

1296
01:06:49.916 --> 01:06:51.958
I mean. even my pets are gone.

1297
01:06:52.541 --> 01:06:54.125
If you want. we can go find them.

1298
01:06:54.208 --> 01:06:56.583
Let them be.
they're better off without me.

1299
01:06:56.916 --> 01:06:58.333
You don't seem so bad to me.

1300
01:06:58.416 --> 01:07:00.458
Nobody seems bad to you.

1301
01:07:00.541 --> 01:07:01.583
And you're not alone

1302
01:07:01.666 --> 01:07:03.208
because you're a Greenbuddie.

1303
01:07:03.833 --> 01:07:05.125
No offense. but...

1304
01:07:05.208 --> 01:07:06.666
What use is that to me now?

1305
01:07:09.916 --> 01:07:11.250
This is Kyle McGregor.

1306
01:07:11.333 --> 01:07:13.458
volunteer number 3459.

1307
01:07:13.541 --> 01:07:15.208
I have an ecological emergency.

1308
01:07:15.291 --> 01:07:16.666
Activate the Alpha protocol.

1309
01:07:17.541 --> 01:07:18.500
What?

1310
01:07:38.541 --> 01:07:42.041
It better be important. I'm missing
pilates because of this call.

1311
01:07:45.958 --> 01:07:48.250
Read them and weep: four aces!

1312
01:07:48.500 --> 01:07:49.416
Cough up the money.

1313
01:07:49.500 --> 01:07:51.916
You're taking advantage
that we don't know how to count!

1314
01:07:52.000 --> 01:07:52.958
Making me think.

1315
01:07:53.041 --> 01:07:54.083
My brain hurts!

1316
01:07:54.166 --> 01:07:57.291
It's impressive to see everything
you've accomplished on your own. madam.

1317
01:07:57.375 --> 01:07:58.291
That’s doctor.

1318
01:07:58.375 --> 01:08:00.916
Have you ever thought about working
for a private company?

1319
01:08:01.208 --> 01:08:03.750
Just think of all the things that
SheetCorp could offer you.

1320
01:08:03.833 --> 01:08:06.375
Like unlimited resources.
cutting-edge technology...

1321
01:08:06.541 --> 01:08:09.250
And the coffee selection at the bar
is just awesome.

1322
01:08:09.333 --> 01:08:10.708
I bet that’s really good.

1323
01:08:10.791 --> 01:08:13.000
But I'll wait a bit. in case you
get jail time for kidnapping.

1324
01:08:14.208 --> 01:08:16.916
Jail time is for the poor. madam.
I'm sure you know that.

1325
01:08:17.000 --> 01:08:17.875
It’s doctor.

1326
01:08:18.041 --> 01:08:19.541
Whatever you say.

1327
01:08:23.083 --> 01:08:24.833
Hey! Get the mechanic over here.

1328
01:08:24.916 --> 01:08:26.833
I think some of the parts
are falling off.

1329
01:08:27.000 --> 01:08:28.625
That's not what you think it is.

1330
01:08:38.416 --> 01:08:39.833
What's all this noise?

1331
01:08:40.000 --> 01:08:41.416
Is a monkey flying this thing or what?

1332
01:08:41.500 --> 01:08:43.375
I think it's a marsupial. sir.

1333
01:08:43.458 --> 01:08:46.083
You don’t say?
What is that rodent doing in here?

1334
01:08:46.166 --> 01:08:48.875
He wants the jellies. sir.
but they’re mine.

1335
01:08:49.625 --> 01:08:51.041
No. stop!

1336
01:09:03.916 --> 01:09:05.125
Useless furball!

1337
01:09:06.416 --> 01:09:08.625
You should have stayed in Australia!

1338
01:09:09.958 --> 01:09:11.291
What are you doing!?

1339
01:09:12.708 --> 01:09:13.916
Yuck!

1340
01:09:18.625 --> 01:09:20.375
Aha! That’s enough!

1341
01:09:20.708 --> 01:09:22.583
7000 people on my staff

1342
01:09:22.666 --> 01:09:25.083
and I still have to do
everything myself.

1343
01:09:26.875 --> 01:09:28.166
Hey?

1344
01:09:29.000 --> 01:09:31.125
Oh you snuck in here with a fuzz-bud!

1345
01:09:31.375 --> 01:09:32.916
You’re not getting the best of me!

1346
01:09:33.000 --> 01:09:34.083
Forget it!

1347
01:09:38.708 --> 01:09:40.416
Just leave those lights alone!

1348
01:09:47.083 --> 01:09:49.708
When we get home
I’m sending both of you to the zoo!

1349
01:10:01.750 --> 01:10:03.166
No. no!

1350
01:10:09.916 --> 01:10:11.208
No!

1351
01:10:12.083 --> 01:10:14.916
You lousy sticking vermin!

1352
01:10:33.750 --> 01:10:35.083
Peggy. we’re alive.

1353
01:10:35.250 --> 01:10:36.666
By some miracle.

1354
01:10:36.958 --> 01:10:38.833
Sir. we can't locate the animals.

1355
01:10:38.916 --> 01:10:41.291
We’re better off without them!
Get the rest of the gear.

1356
01:10:41.375 --> 01:10:42.708
You’ll continue on foot.

1357
01:10:43.083 --> 01:10:44.708
Come on. everybody up!

1358
01:11:05.166 --> 01:11:08.916
And the last time.
I lost all flexibility in my core.

1359
01:11:09.166 --> 01:11:11.416
From one week to the next.
boom. gone.

1360
01:11:11.750 --> 01:11:13.333
Hey. you listening to me?

1361
01:11:13.666 --> 01:11:16.291
Yo. microwave!
I'm opening my heart to you here!

1362
01:11:21.333 --> 01:11:24.041
Wow. this microwave
isn’t useless after all.

1363
01:11:25.125 --> 01:11:26.291
Okay. we're getting close!

1364
01:11:26.375 --> 01:11:27.125
Seat belts! Now!

1365
01:11:30.375 --> 01:11:33.541
Are you sure we can land
without this thing falling apart?

1366
01:11:33.625 --> 01:11:35.041
Excuse me.

1367
01:11:35.208 --> 01:11:37.750
are you a pilot with
thousands of hours of flight time

1368
01:11:37.833 --> 01:11:41.208
and decades of experience
in countless extreme rescues?

1369
01:11:41.291 --> 01:11:42.458
Ehm... No.

1370
01:11:42.625 --> 01:11:45.541
Well then. how about you let me
worry about the landing?

1371
01:11:51.708 --> 01:11:53.333
Are you sure you’re related to her?

1372
01:11:53.416 --> 01:11:55.333
Uh-huh.
She’s my aunt and my dad's sister.

1373
01:11:55.625 --> 01:11:56.583
Both.

1374
01:11:56.666 --> 01:11:58.458
Oh my god.
What a pain in the rear.

1375
01:11:58.875 --> 01:12:00.041
Well. we’re almost there.

1376
01:12:00.125 --> 01:12:01.708
Maybe it’s just a misunderstanding.

1377
01:12:01.875 --> 01:12:03.458
I saw my parents get kidnapped.

1378
01:12:03.541 --> 01:12:05.166
What’s confusing to you about that?

1379
01:12:05.250 --> 01:12:07.416
They could have been kidnapped
by mistake?

1380
01:12:07.500 --> 01:12:10.625
Kyle. this may surprise you
but not everyone can be trusted.

1381
01:12:10.708 --> 01:12:12.041
You have to set boundaries.

1382
01:12:12.125 --> 01:12:13.416
people take advantage of you.

1383
01:12:14.916 --> 01:12:16.875
Nobody takes advantage of me!

1384
01:12:18.500 --> 01:12:19.375
Really? They do?

1385
01:12:19.791 --> 01:12:21.541
-Oh. no!
-Oh. yes.

1386
01:12:21.625 --> 01:12:23.916
The sooner you accept it.
the sooner you can start...

1387
01:12:24.083 --> 01:12:25.541
Smoke! Over there!

1388
01:12:26.958 --> 01:12:27.958
Oh. no!

1389
01:12:37.375 --> 01:12:39.333
There's no one inside.
which is a good sign.

1390
01:12:39.416 --> 01:12:40.583
What's that? Look!

1391
01:12:43.708 --> 01:12:44.958
My pets!

1392
01:12:46.041 --> 01:12:48.166
They must have come in the helicopter!

1393
01:12:48.250 --> 01:12:50.500
They were super lucky
to survive the accident.

1394
01:12:50.666 --> 01:12:52.666
I wouldn’t be surprised
if they caused it.

1395
01:12:52.750 --> 01:12:56.083
-Alright. what do we do now?
-How about following those tracks?

1396
01:12:56.625 --> 01:12:57.666
Let's go!

1397
01:13:03.375 --> 01:13:05.750
Yeah. good idea. Robert. Onward!

1398
01:13:24.708 --> 01:13:26.458
I'm just saying we should take turns.

1399
01:13:26.541 --> 01:13:28.125
I’m uncomfortable walking backwards

1400
01:13:28.208 --> 01:13:30.500
and I feel like I'm missing
the best of the scenery.

1401
01:13:33.791 --> 01:13:34.833
Aha!

1402
01:13:36.958 --> 01:13:38.041
Wow.

1403
01:13:38.958 --> 01:13:40.500
Wow? Wow what?

1404
01:13:40.583 --> 01:13:42.291
Hey. hey. hey. hey! Slow down!

1405
01:13:43.750 --> 01:13:44.833
Wow.

1406
01:13:46.250 --> 01:13:48.250
What's going on?
What is it?

1407
01:13:48.333 --> 01:13:50.291
I'm missing out on the good stuff.
aren’t I?

1408
01:13:50.708 --> 01:13:52.250
Let me see!

1409
01:13:52.625 --> 01:13:53.541
Gordon!

1410
01:14:11.875 --> 01:14:13.041
Wow!

1411
01:14:26.916 --> 01:14:28.000
Oh my goodness...

1412
01:14:28.083 --> 01:14:30.791
the animals have been feeding
on those berries for centuries.

1413
01:14:30.875 --> 01:14:32.416
mutating their genes.

1414
01:14:32.500 --> 01:14:34.208
That's why they don't migrate.

1415
01:14:34.291 --> 01:14:35.333
They mutate.

1416
01:14:35.416 --> 01:14:37.166
they’ve adapted to climate change.

1417
01:14:37.333 --> 01:14:39.291
From a scientific point of view. it's...

1418
01:14:39.375 --> 01:14:40.958
Completely meaningless gibberish?

1419
01:14:41.041 --> 01:14:41.958
Exactly.

1420
01:14:42.041 --> 01:14:44.708
Although the appropriate
term would be... Magic!

1421
01:14:48.333 --> 01:14:49.625
You know?
I'm no expert.

1422
01:14:49.708 --> 01:14:51.541
but shouldn't they be eating each other?

1423
01:14:53.708 --> 01:14:55.541
Gordon. you're right!

1424
01:14:55.833 --> 01:14:58.333
But instead they help one another.

1425
01:14:58.583 --> 01:15:01.000
care for each other
and protect each other!

1426
01:15:01.083 --> 01:15:03.166
The tree gives them
everything they need.

1427
01:15:03.250 --> 01:15:05.083
so they have learned
to trust each other!

1428
01:15:05.166 --> 01:15:07.791
That's why adrenaline inhibits
the effects of the berries!

1429
01:15:07.875 --> 01:15:08.833
They know no fear!

1430
01:15:08.916 --> 01:15:10.625
It's a perfect ecosystem!

1431
01:15:11.625 --> 01:15:12.625
Wow.

1432
01:15:12.708 --> 01:15:15.500
It's the most beautiful thing
I've ever seen...

1433
01:15:15.666 --> 01:15:17.333
I want it for myself.

1434
01:15:17.666 --> 01:15:19.583
Cage up the animals.
and sample everything!

1435
01:15:19.666 --> 01:15:20.583
Move it!

1436
01:15:41.916 --> 01:15:44.208
It's... extraordinary.

1437
01:15:46.500 --> 01:15:48.875
The ultimate life energy will be mine!

1438
01:15:48.958 --> 01:15:51.208
I’ll have the power of a god!

1439
01:15:51.625 --> 01:15:54.333
And it'll look just great
on our rooftop garden!

1440
01:15:54.416 --> 01:15:55.916
What? You can't take it!

1441
01:15:56.000 --> 01:15:57.541
You'll destroy the ecosystem!

1442
01:15:57.916 --> 01:15:59.333
You know that I'm rich. madam.

1443
01:15:59.416 --> 01:16:01.291
I can do whatever I want.

1444
01:16:06.791 --> 01:16:08.416
Freeze. little bugger!

1445
01:16:11.041 --> 01:16:12.250
He's being protective.

1446
01:16:12.333 --> 01:16:13.625
he knows they depend on it!

1447
01:16:13.708 --> 01:16:14.791
Who. TJ?

1448
01:16:14.875 --> 01:16:16.208
No! The walrus bear!

1449
01:16:16.291 --> 01:16:18.416
You mean the walrus bear
is protecting TJ?

1450
01:16:18.500 --> 01:16:20.750
No! He's protecting the tree from TJ

1451
01:16:20.916 --> 01:16:21.875
because they depend on it.

1452
01:16:21.958 --> 01:16:24.083
-So the tree depends on TJ?
-Will you just zip it?

1453
01:16:24.291 --> 01:16:25.625
I'm missing it because of you!

1454
01:16:25.708 --> 01:16:27.708
But of course.
You're missing it!

1455
01:16:35.125 --> 01:16:36.833
I don't have time for this junk.

1456
01:16:40.500 --> 01:16:42.916
Now you're mine...

1457
01:16:48.333 --> 01:16:51.166
Oh...
He wants to protect his little tree.

1458
01:16:51.250 --> 01:16:52.125
oh my.

1459
01:16:52.208 --> 01:16:54.250
Isn't that simply adorable?

1460
01:16:56.458 --> 01:16:58.000
No. it's not.

1461
01:16:58.500 --> 01:16:59.500
Stay out of my way.

1462
01:16:59.583 --> 01:17:01.333
you ridiculous furry tadpole.

1463
01:17:10.916 --> 01:17:12.250
Hashtag save the Arctic.

1464
01:17:12.333 --> 01:17:13.458
hashtag biodiversity.

1465
01:17:13.541 --> 01:17:15.375
Blah. blah. blah. blah. blah. blah...

1466
01:17:21.833 --> 01:17:23.083
He made him cry!

1467
01:17:23.458 --> 01:17:25.333
Is he like... a bad person?

1468
01:17:25.416 --> 01:17:27.583
Good.
Finally getting it. my nephew.

1469
01:17:27.666 --> 01:17:29.416
Oh. I see my parents! There!

1470
01:17:33.958 --> 01:17:35.791
Come on. we have to rescue them!

1471
01:17:36.333 --> 01:17:37.708
Zoe. wait!

1472
01:17:41.125 --> 01:17:43.958
I have so many plans for the two of us.

1473
01:17:45.458 --> 01:17:46.750
It's all yours.

1474
01:18:08.666 --> 01:18:10.166
No. no. no. no. no. no...

1475
01:18:10.250 --> 01:18:11.458
What are you doing?

1476
01:18:16.291 --> 01:18:17.583
What's going on here?

1477
01:18:19.041 --> 01:18:21.083
Where did all these creatures come from?

1478
01:18:28.083 --> 01:18:29.666
Well. like the old saying goes.

1479
01:18:29.750 --> 01:18:31.250
if you can't beat 'em. then...

1480
01:18:33.125 --> 01:18:35.416
No! That's way. way too much!

1481
01:18:35.500 --> 01:18:37.250
Way too much of what?

1482
01:19:00.875 --> 01:19:02.041
That's enough.

1483
01:19:02.125 --> 01:19:04.333
I need to see what’s going on here.

1484
01:19:11.458 --> 01:19:12.958
On second thought... Oop...

1485
01:19:13.708 --> 01:19:14.833
Maybe not.

1486
01:19:18.916 --> 01:19:21.333
Ha!
I almost missed this because of pilates.

1487
01:19:22.125 --> 01:19:24.583
Hey! What are you girls doing here?

1488
01:19:24.666 --> 01:19:27.166
Excuse me.
do you have a minute to save the planet?

1489
01:19:27.250 --> 01:19:28.416
Can't you see I'm busy?

1490
01:19:29.791 --> 01:19:30.541
Calm down!

1491
01:19:30.625 --> 01:19:32.458
We're from an environmental organization

1492
01:19:32.541 --> 01:19:34.583
fighting to save the planet from...

1493
01:19:34.916 --> 01:19:36.708
I already belong to several NGOs!

1494
01:19:36.875 --> 01:19:38.375
I can't afford another one!

1495
01:19:38.916 --> 01:19:41.416
That's what you always say
and it's always a lie!

1496
01:19:41.583 --> 01:19:43.375
Run. Zoe! Save your parents!

1497
01:19:43.541 --> 01:19:44.416
Alone?

1498
01:19:44.500 --> 01:19:46.791
I think I’ll wait for you!

1499
01:19:46.958 --> 01:19:47.916
Robert. no!

1500
01:19:49.791 --> 01:19:51.833
Careful. careful. aaahhh!

1501
01:19:56.416 --> 01:19:57.416
Come to Daddy.

1502
01:19:58.666 --> 01:20:00.500
Huh? Not you again.

1503
01:20:00.583 --> 01:20:01.791
Get out of here!

1504
01:20:01.875 --> 01:20:03.083
Do you have any idea

1505
01:20:03.166 --> 01:20:05.083
who you're messing with. huh?

1506
01:20:11.666 --> 01:20:13.916
W-w-w... What?!

1507
01:20:15.000 --> 01:20:16.583
This is absolutely the end!

1508
01:20:20.083 --> 01:20:21.791
What do you want me to do?

1509
01:20:21.875 --> 01:20:24.833
He's a 50-foot monster.
and I'm a 12 year old girl!

1510
01:20:24.916 --> 01:20:26.333
Hey!

1511
01:20:39.875 --> 01:20:41.208
Robert! Are you alright?

1512
01:20:44.416 --> 01:20:45.333
The berries!

1513
01:20:47.208 --> 01:20:48.583
Aaahhh...

1514
01:20:49.000 --> 01:20:51.291
Are you all thinking what I’m thinking?

1515
01:20:51.916 --> 01:20:54.291
Whatever. it can't get any worse.

1516
01:20:56.416 --> 01:20:57.458
It’s incredible!

1517
01:20:57.541 --> 01:21:00.500
The morphological assimilation
is both immediate and cumulative!

1518
01:21:00.583 --> 01:21:02.291
Yes. yes. yes.
very interesting.

1519
01:21:02.375 --> 01:21:04.000
but we have to get out of here.

1520
01:21:06.708 --> 01:21:08.416
Can't you see that monster
is going to crush us?!

1521
01:21:08.583 --> 01:21:11.083
As long as he pays.
that monster can do whatever wants.

1522
01:21:11.583 --> 01:21:12.500
Excuse me.

1523
01:21:12.583 --> 01:21:13.916
Omega Team. Report.

1524
01:21:14.083 --> 01:21:15.083
We found a monkey.

1525
01:21:15.166 --> 01:21:16.791
He says he's lost and cold.

1526
01:21:16.875 --> 01:21:18.750
A monkey?
A talking monkey?

1527
01:21:18.833 --> 01:21:20.875
Affirmative.
He's pretty adorable.

1528
01:21:20.958 --> 01:21:23.083
Requesting permission
to lend it a jacke...eeagh!

1529
01:21:23.166 --> 01:21:24.333
Omega... Omega Team?

1530
01:21:24.416 --> 01:21:25.958
-Get that thing away!
-Report!

1531
01:21:26.250 --> 01:21:27.458
What’s going on?

1532
01:21:27.625 --> 01:21:28.666
We're under attack!

1533
01:21:35.750 --> 01:21:37.375
Aaah!

1534
01:21:37.458 --> 01:21:39.458
It's coming!
It's coming!

1535
01:21:39.541 --> 01:21:41.250
Aaah!

1536
01:21:46.333 --> 01:21:49.166
Release my parents right now.
or else...

1537
01:21:49.666 --> 01:21:51.125
Or else what?

1538
01:21:51.333 --> 01:21:52.458
Or else...

1539
01:21:53.458 --> 01:21:54.291
Or else...

1540
01:21:54.541 --> 01:21:56.333
Uhm. just a second. okay?

1541
01:21:58.625 --> 01:21:59.750
Get it. get it!

1542
01:22:00.041 --> 01:22:00.958
Come on.

1543
01:22:02.208 --> 01:22:03.458
go get it!

1544
01:22:16.458 --> 01:22:18.625
Okay. enough of this nonsense.

1545
01:22:19.875 --> 01:22:22.125
Huh?
Hey. you. come back here!

1546
01:22:22.291 --> 01:22:23.750
Heeey!

1547
01:22:27.333 --> 01:22:29.541
Why can't I catch that stupid thing?

1548
01:22:29.833 --> 01:22:31.791
Just leave it. don’t worry about it!

1549
01:22:31.875 --> 01:22:32.916
Calm down!

1550
01:22:33.166 --> 01:22:34.458
I'm fine.
I'm fine.

1551
01:22:34.541 --> 01:22:35.500
-Zoe!
-Zoe!

1552
01:22:42.541 --> 01:22:44.750
Did you become an animal again?
What were you thinking?

1553
01:22:44.833 --> 01:22:47.250
You can punish her later. no phone!
How did you get here?

1554
01:22:47.333 --> 01:22:48.708
We came by plane.
It’s over there!

1555
01:22:48.875 --> 01:22:50.375
Whose plane? Do I know them?

1556
01:22:50.458 --> 01:22:51.666
Outstanding!

1557
01:22:51.750 --> 01:22:53.500
I was starting to worry
about getting home.

1558
01:22:53.583 --> 01:22:54.708
Maybe somewhere will be open.

1559
01:22:54.875 --> 01:22:56.000
Fancy some sushi?

1560
01:22:56.458 --> 01:22:57.541
No!

1561
01:23:01.958 --> 01:23:03.750
Don't you remember what the mouse said?

1562
01:23:03.833 --> 01:23:05.875
The tree is the source of life!

1563
01:23:10.041 --> 01:23:11.791
Just a little more!

1564
01:23:15.416 --> 01:23:16.958
We have to stop TJ!

1565
01:23:17.041 --> 01:23:18.708
Mom. do you have more of the antidote?

1566
01:23:18.791 --> 01:23:19.750
I only have one dose left.

1567
01:23:19.916 --> 01:23:22.166
Awesome. You guys go free the animals.

1568
01:23:22.250 --> 01:23:24.000
meanwhile you distract TJ.

1569
01:23:24.083 --> 01:23:26.208
I'll climb the tree and... aaagh!

1570
01:23:26.291 --> 01:23:27.583
Mom! What have you done?

1571
01:23:27.666 --> 01:23:29.208
That was the last dose.

1572
01:23:29.291 --> 01:23:31.666
You think I’m going to let you
stay an animal forever?

1573
01:23:31.750 --> 01:23:32.916
What about the tree?

1574
01:23:33.000 --> 01:23:34.250
What do you want us to do?

1575
01:23:34.416 --> 01:23:35.750
We don't have anymore antidote!

1576
01:23:58.708 --> 01:23:59.958
Aaaaaah!

1577
01:24:03.583 --> 01:24:05.708
I have an idea.
but it's dangerous.

1578
01:24:05.791 --> 01:24:07.458
I don't have time to explain it.

1579
01:24:07.541 --> 01:24:09.208
You have to trust me. alright?

1580
01:24:09.291 --> 01:24:10.291
-Yes.
-Sure.

1581
01:24:12.208 --> 01:24:13.166
Go for it.

1582
01:24:13.250 --> 01:24:15.166
If you think it's a good idea.
so do I.

1583
01:24:17.333 --> 01:24:18.083
Zoe...

1584
01:24:18.166 --> 01:24:19.750
Try not to mess it up.

1585
01:24:20.041 --> 01:24:21.333
I promise you.

1586
01:24:21.416 --> 01:24:22.541
Free the animals.

1587
01:24:22.625 --> 01:24:24.291
Robert. here we go!

1588
01:24:27.041 --> 01:24:30.166
Come on. you have got this... Huh?

1589
01:24:31.458 --> 01:24:33.416
-Hey!
-What are you doing here?

1590
01:24:33.500 --> 01:24:34.750
Do you actually think

1591
01:24:34.833 --> 01:24:36.041
people will love you more

1592
01:24:36.125 --> 01:24:37.208
because you're powerful?

1593
01:24:37.291 --> 01:24:40.333
That you really have to destroy
everything to get their attention?!

1594
01:24:40.500 --> 01:24:42.333
Guess what.
I used to think the same way

1595
01:24:42.416 --> 01:24:43.375
but I was wrong.

1596
01:24:43.458 --> 01:24:45.583
You don't have to break stuff
and shout louder

1597
01:24:45.666 --> 01:24:46.791
if you want attention.

1598
01:24:46.875 --> 01:24:49.416
You gotta try to get along with people

1599
01:24:49.500 --> 01:24:51.833
You know.
you’re not the only person in the world!

1600
01:24:57.541 --> 01:24:59.750
Do you really think
you're going to convince me

1601
01:24:59.833 --> 01:25:01.291
with some corny monologue?

1602
01:25:01.375 --> 01:25:03.583
No. I just wanted to buy some time.

1603
01:25:04.083 --> 01:25:06.083
Some time? Time for what?

1604
01:25:10.041 --> 01:25:11.000
Beep.

1605
01:25:13.083 --> 01:25:16.000
Oh my. Isn't that simply adorable?

1606
01:25:16.083 --> 01:25:17.625
No. it's not.

1607
01:25:17.708 --> 01:25:20.041
Stay out of my way.
you ridiculous furry tadpole.

1608
01:25:20.583 --> 01:25:22.000
And why should I care?!

1609
01:25:22.083 --> 01:25:24.166
We just uploaded that video
to the internet

1610
01:25:24.250 --> 01:25:26.625
and I bet you anything it's a huge hit.

1611
01:25:26.708 --> 01:25:27.791
And you wanna know why?

1612
01:25:27.875 --> 01:25:30.333
Because the world likes
the curious and the kind.

1613
01:25:30.416 --> 01:25:31.833
not brutes like you.

1614
01:25:31.916 --> 01:25:34.541
Who can talk like that
to something so adorable?

1615
01:25:34.625 --> 01:25:36.708
If I get my hands on him.
he'll be sorry!

1616
01:25:36.791 --> 01:25:38.083
He's a monster! What a bully!

1617
01:25:38.291 --> 01:25:40.208
He's a nobody!
Don't buy his products!

1618
01:25:40.291 --> 01:25:42.625
No. no. no. no. no...

1619
01:25:45.375 --> 01:25:46.708
No!

1620
01:25:52.083 --> 01:25:54.750
Ow. ow. ow!

1621
01:25:56.125 --> 01:25:57.416
Zoe! You did it!

1622
01:25:57.500 --> 01:25:59.041
You were amazing. sweetheart!

1623
01:25:59.833 --> 01:26:02.041
-I am so proud of you!
-I am so proud of you!

1624
01:26:05.333 --> 01:26:06.208
Yes!

1625
01:26:06.583 --> 01:26:07.625
Big hug!

1626
01:26:13.750 --> 01:26:15.833
Go on! They’re waiting for you.

1627
01:26:19.583 --> 01:26:20.583
Good Luck!

1628
01:26:21.208 --> 01:26:23.875
Hey. you. kid.
You gotta help me out here.

1629
01:26:23.958 --> 01:26:26.125
This whole thing's
been a total misunderstanding.

1630
01:26:26.208 --> 01:26:28.875
I wasn’t trying
to take the tree down. no. no.

1631
01:26:28.958 --> 01:26:30.208
I was just trying to move it

1632
01:26:30.291 --> 01:26:31.708
so it could get more light.

1633
01:26:31.791 --> 01:26:32.708
Oh. really?

1634
01:26:32.791 --> 01:26:35.250
Sure. wait until we explain
everything to Zoe.

1635
01:26:35.333 --> 01:26:36.791
she'll be so relieved to hear that.

1636
01:26:36.958 --> 01:26:38.875
No. no. no. no. no. no. Leave her alone.

1637
01:26:38.958 --> 01:26:41.500
What I need is for you
to give me the keys to the plane

1638
01:26:41.583 --> 01:26:42.666
for just a minute.

1639
01:26:42.750 --> 01:26:44.666
You know. to warm up from the cold.

1640
01:26:44.750 --> 01:26:46.125
Sure. of course.

1641
01:26:47.666 --> 01:26:48.916
Wow! Hold on...

1642
01:26:49.000 --> 01:26:50.833
you're trying to trick me. aren't you?

1643
01:26:51.000 --> 01:26:53.208
Eh... No...

1644
01:26:54.625 --> 01:26:56.041
Congratulations. nephew.

1645
01:26:56.125 --> 01:26:57.291
Looks like you’ve got it.

1646
01:26:57.375 --> 01:26:59.833
All I ever wanted to do
is help humanity.

1647
01:26:59.916 --> 01:27:02.333
To help us take the next step
in our evolution.

1648
01:27:02.500 --> 01:27:03.500
And you still can.

1649
01:27:03.583 --> 01:27:05.333
Have you heard of Greenbuddies?

1650
01:27:36.750 --> 01:27:38.208
I have something to tell you.

1651
01:27:38.541 --> 01:27:40.625
I love you and I want us to get along.

1652
01:27:40.708 --> 01:27:42.291
and that's why...

1653
01:27:42.500 --> 01:27:45.375
Maybe boarding school
isn't such a bad idea after all.

1654
01:27:45.458 --> 01:27:47.500
I could use a little discipline.

1655
01:27:47.583 --> 01:27:48.500
Okay honey.

1656
01:27:48.583 --> 01:27:51.041
as soon as we see a mailbox.
we'll send in the form.

1657
01:27:51.125 --> 01:27:52.750
Robert. can you take care of this?

1658
01:27:54.708 --> 01:27:56.208
Mom! What are you...

1659
01:28:00.666 --> 01:28:02.958
What do you say we go camping instead?
Or to the beach.

1660
01:28:03.041 --> 01:28:04.291
Or camping at the beach.

1661
01:28:06.166 --> 01:28:07.333
That's the spirit.

1662
01:28:07.416 --> 01:28:08.708
If she wants boarding school.

1663
01:28:08.791 --> 01:28:10.416
she can pay for it herself.

1664
01:28:12.666 --> 01:28:14.625
Are you thinking what I’m thinking?

1665
01:28:15.041 --> 01:28:17.583
-Salvatica.
-Salvatica.

1666
01:28:22.666 --> 01:28:25.541
Zoe. we've decided
we're going to stay here.

1667
01:28:25.625 --> 01:28:27.375
Stay here? Are you kidding?

1668
01:28:27.458 --> 01:28:29.416
No. We're going to trust our instincts.

1669
01:28:29.500 --> 01:28:31.375
Awaken our inner animal.

1670
01:28:31.458 --> 01:28:32.833
Defy the the status quo.

1671
01:28:32.916 --> 01:28:34.958
Whatever the heck that means.
I don’t know.

1672
01:28:35.125 --> 01:28:36.625
But this isn't your habitat.

1673
01:28:36.708 --> 01:28:38.083
How are you going to manage?

1674
01:28:38.750 --> 01:28:40.458
If we’ve survived life as humans.

1675
01:28:40.541 --> 01:28:42.166
we can survive anything.

1676
01:28:44.375 --> 01:28:46.208
If you think it's a good idea...

1677
01:28:46.291 --> 01:28:47.500
then so do I.

1678
01:28:51.125 --> 01:28:53.000
But I'm going to miss you so much.

1679
01:28:53.083 --> 01:28:54.708
And we'll miss you.

1680
01:28:54.791 --> 01:28:57.458
You can come visit us anytime.

1681
01:28:57.541 --> 01:28:59.500
Go on.
Before I get all emotional here.

1682
01:29:14.875 --> 01:29:17.083
A FEW WEEKS LATER

1683
01:29:26.250 --> 01:29:27.625
That was beyond awful!

1684
01:29:27.708 --> 01:29:29.958
Enough roughing it.
what's for dinner?

1685
01:29:30.041 --> 01:29:31.125
Tell me you have a charger.

1686
01:29:31.208 --> 01:29:33.083
-Dibs on the bathtub!
-Any pizza left?

1687
01:29:33.166 --> 01:29:34.166
Blanket and movie!

1688
01:29:34.250 --> 01:29:36.083
Wow. this hair needs some conditioner.

1689
01:29:36.583 --> 01:29:38.625
Hey there. kiddo.
ready to go?

1690
01:29:39.291 --> 01:29:40.166
Oh!

1691
01:29:41.291 --> 01:29:42.166
Big hug.

1692
01:29:44.375 --> 01:29:45.666
Ready for another beating?

1693
01:29:45.750 --> 01:29:46.750
Always!

1694
01:29:47.333 --> 01:29:50.250
Your little friends are here?
What happened to back to nature?

1695
01:29:50.791 --> 01:29:52.041
Well. maybe...

1696
01:29:53.000 --> 01:29:55.541
It just wasn't as cool as they expected.

1697
01:29:55.625 --> 01:29:57.041
Oh. poor things...

1698
01:29:57.125 --> 01:29:59.375
Anyway. to err is human.

1699
01:30:02.458 --> 01:30:04.666
THE END

1699
01:30:05.305 --> 01:31:05.208
